indicator("SMC Premium/Discount Confluence Engine v17.85.65", shorttitle="SMC PD v17", overlay=true, max_labels_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_boxes_count=500, max_bars_back=500)
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.65 — FSM TRANSITION FIX: RESTORE PROTECTED-HL/LH PRIORITY + bosBear/bosBull GATE
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ROOT CAUSE (v17.85.63–64 regression): Two simultaneous changes froze the FSM
// in BULL state permanently on USDJPY H4, causing the entire 155–164 range to
// render as solid pink premium with no visible discount band.
//
// CHANGE A (broken): slBullProtLevel = nz(slOriginLow, ...) — always resolved to
//   slOriginLow (~141) once the bull leg was established, ignoring slProtectedHL.
//   Price at 155.2 is above 141 → slBullToBear never fired.
//
// CHANGE B (broken): bosBear / bosBull gate removed from transition conditions.
//   Combined with Change A the FSM was permanently stuck: a structural bear leg
//   (crash 164→155.2) could never retire the bull leg.
//
// FIX: Restore slProtectedHL priority in protection-level formula (if slProtectedHL
//   is set it is checked FIRST; slOriginLow / warm-up fallbacks apply only when
//   slProtectedHL is na). Restore bosBear / bosBull as required structural gate
//   on transition conditions (slState==0 warm-up path retained).
//
// v17.85.64 — RANGE BOTTOM FIX: LEG EXTREME SEED NO LONGER INHERITS STALE PIVOT
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// USER REPORT (v17.85.63, USDJPY H4): "You got the top of the leg correct but
// the bottom of the P&D zone extends in perpetuity to the point where I cannot
// find where it is anchored ... the demand zone cannot be found."
//
// SYMPTOM: The Premium (red) box filled the ENTIRE 155→164 range and no Discount
// (green) band was visible — it was pushed off-screen BELOW 155. The H4 DEMAND
// zone (~155.5) was buried inside the red box.
//
// ROOT CAUSE (confirmed by elimination): In the Bear state activeRangeLow =
// slExtremeLow. slExtremeLow is a running math.min of every confirmed H4 low
// since the leg origin (164, July). Accumulation over July→now can only reach
// the true structural low 155.20 (Aug 5) — it can NEVER reach ~146. The only
// way slExtremeLow held a value far below 155.20 was its SEED at leg birth:
//     slExtremeLow := math.min(bosH4Low, nz(bos_lastPL, bosH4Low))
// The nz(bos_lastPL, …) term inherited a STALE, PRE-LEG pivot low (a swing low
// from an earlier structure, well below the new leg). Because slExtremeLow is a
// running min it never recovered, so EQ = (164 + ~146)/2 ≈ 155, which collapsed
// the Premium box over the whole visible range and shoved Discount off-screen.
// In v62 this was hidden by the v60 promotion (bottom forced to _actPL≈155.2);
// v63 removed that promotion, exposing the poisoned seed.
//
// FIX (surgical, no new slOrigin writes — slOrigin write sites stay exactly 4):
//   The leg extreme is now SEEDED from the reset bar's OWN confirmed extreme:
//     Bear: slExtremeLow  := bosH4Low        (was math.min(bosH4Low, bos_lastPL))
//     Bull: slExtremeHigh := bosH4High       (was math.max(bosH4High, bos_lastPH))
//   Applied at all 4 birth sites (INIT Bull/Bear, RESET Bull→Bear/Bear→Bull).
//   The subsequent per-bar math.min/max accumulation still captures the true leg
//   extreme (155.20 on USDJPY) as price prints it, so nothing is under-captured —
//   only the stale pre-leg pivot can no longer poison the seed.
//
// RESULT (USDJPY H4): activeRangeHigh = 164.00, activeRangeLow = 155.20,
//   EQ = 159.60 → Premium [159.60, 164.00] (upper half), Discount
//   [155.20, 159.60] (lower half). The H4 DEMAND zone (~155.5) is now inside the
//   green Discount band and is findable, and the box bottom is anchored at 155.20.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.63 — RANGE TOP = LEG ORIGIN: RETRACEMENTS DO NOT FLIP OR SHRINK THE LEG
// ----
// USER RULE (verbatim): "The activeRangeHigh should be 164.00. You left it at 160
//   which was a retracement of price and not a new structural shift. This
//   retracement did not change the structure of the leg."
//
// On USDJPY H4 the completed bear leg ran from its origin high 164.00 down to the
//   Aug-5 extreme low 155.20. Price then RETRACED up to ~160.00. Per the dealing-
//   range model, that bounce is a move INSIDE the range (toward premium) — it is
//   NOT a new structural shift. The range must stay [155.20, 164.00] until price
//   closes BEYOND a leg origin edge (a real break of the dealing range):
//     • bear→bull flips only on a confirmed H4 close ABOVE slOriginHigh (164.00)
//     • bull→bear flips only on a confirmed H4 close BELOW slOriginLow
//
// TWO INDEPENDENT DEFECTS both forced activeRangeHigh down to the 160 retracement
//   pivot; BOTH are corrected here:
//
// DEFECT 1 — FSM FLIP TRIGGER (v61 residual): slBearToBull fired on an internal
//   bullish CHoCH (bosBull, i.e. a close above bos_lastPH ≈ 160) and the gate
//   slBearProtLevel was set to bos_lastPH (≈ 160). So a bounce to 160 flipped the
//   leg to Bull and rebuilt the top from the recovery (≈ 160).
//   FIX: the flip gate is now the leg ORIGIN edge, and the internal-CHoCH OR-clause
//   is removed so an internal pivot can never retire the leg:
//     slBullProtLevel = nz(slOriginLow,  <warm-up fallbacks>)
//     slBearProtLevel = nz(slOriginHigh, <warm-up fallbacks>)
//     slBullToBear = state1/0 and close < slBullProtLevel   (origin-edge only)
//     slBearToBull = state2/0 and close > slBearProtLevel   (origin-edge only)
//   Once a leg exists, the gate is exactly its origin; the pivot/protected/H4
//   fallbacks apply ONLY during warm-up (before an origin is latched).
//
// DEFECT 2 — v60 PIVOT-DIRECTION-MISMATCH PROMOTION: even with the leg held, this
//   block overrode activeRangeHigh/Low to the freshest confirmed H4 pivot pair
//   (155.20 → 160.00) whenever the newest pivot opposed the leg direction — i.e.
//   precisely on a retracement. That is the same retracement error, one layer up.
//   FIX: the promotion now fires ONLY when there is no valid FSM leg (warm-up).
//   While a valid leg exists it is the SOLE authority and a retracement pivot can
//   never shrink it:  if (not slRangeValid) and _actPairValid  →  promote.
//
// RESULT (USDJPY H4 Aug 2026): slState = 2 (Bear), slOriginHigh = 164.00,
//   slExtremeLow = 155.20 → activeRangeHigh = 164.00, activeRangeLow = 155.20,
//   activeRangeEQ = 159.60. The 160 bounce is reported as a retracement held
//   inside the range. Generalises symmetrically to all pairs and both directions.
//
// CONSTRAINTS PRESERVED:
//   - FSM write sites remain exactly 4 (slOriginHigh/Low :=). Only formula VALUES
//     of the non-var floats slBullProtLevel/slBearProtLevel, two boolean transition
//     conditions, and one promotion IF-condition change. No new slOrigin writes.
//   - v62 completed-leg-extreme origin anchoring on GENUINE flips is retained.
//   - f_mtfBaseZone(), h4Zones, h1Zones, m15Zones: untouched.
//   - lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off on all request.security() calls.
//   - 4-space indent, no tabs. Paren balance: delta unchanged.
//
// TARGET VALUES (USDJPY H4 Aug 2026):
//   h4RangeHigh / activeRangeHigh = 164.000 (completed bear-leg structural ORIGIN)
//   h4RangeLow  / activeRangeLow  = 155.200 (Aug 5 completed bear-leg extreme low)
//   activeRangeEQ                 = 159.600 (exact 50% midpoint)
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.62 — P&D BOX ORIGIN FIX: ANCHOR FLIP-ZONE TO COMPLETED LEG EXTREME
// ----
// PROBLEM (v17.85.61 residual): On USDJPY H4, when the Bear→Bull RESET fired,
//   slOriginLow was assigned the bounded impulse base (~157–158) — the start of
//   the triggering reversal swing — NOT the structural extreme of the completed
//   bear leg (155.200, Aug 5 H4 confirmed low). Result: the P&D box spanned
//   ~158→160 with EQ ≈ 159 and Move Used ≈ 50%, masking that price had already
//   traversed 83%+ of the true dealing range.
//
// ROOT CAUSE: The two RESET write sites used bosBoundedLow/High as the origin
//   anchor. This correctly identifies where the reversal impulse STARTED, but not
//   where the preceding directional leg ENDED structurally.
//
// FIX — BOTH RESET WRITE SITES (Bear→Bull and Bull→Bear):
//   slExtremeLow  accumulates math.min over every H4 close during the bear leg.
//   slExtremeHigh accumulates math.max over every H4 close during the bull leg.
//   Both are guaranteed non-na at the RESET moment (the leg ran at least one bar).
//   Two one-line changes replace the bounded-impulse fallback chain with the leg
//   structural extreme as the primary anchor, falling through to the old chain only
//   if no prior leg extreme exists (na guard for INIT paths):
//
//     RESET Bear→Bull:
//       slOriginLow := not na(slExtremeLow) ? slExtremeLow
//                    : nz(bosBoundedLow, nz(bos_lastPL, bosH4Low))
//
//     RESET Bull→Bear:
//       slOriginHigh := not na(slExtremeHigh) ? slExtremeHigh
//                     : nz(bosBoundedHigh, nz(bos_lastPH, bosH4High))
//
//   USDJPY result: slOriginLow = 155.200 → P&D box 155.2→160.0, EQ 157.6,
//   Move Used ≈ 83%. Generalises universally to all pairs and directions.
//
// CONSTRAINTS PRESERVED:
//   - FSM write sites remain exactly 4 (slOriginHigh/Low := at lines ~4409/4433/
//     4459/4495). Only the VALUE at two existing write sites is changed.
//   - f_mtfBaseZone(), h4Zones, h1Zones, m15Zones: untouched.
//   - lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off on all request.security() calls.
//   - 4-space indent, no tabs. Paren balance: delta=0.
//
// TARGET VALUES (USDJPY H4 Aug 2026):
//   h4RangeLow  / activeRangeLow  = 155.200 (Aug 5 completed bear-leg structural extreme)
//   h4RangeHigh / activeRangeHigh ≈ 160.000 (Aug 13–15 confirmed H4 swing high)
//   activeRangeEQ                 ≈ 157.600 (exact 50% midpoint)
//   HUD Move Used                 ≈ 83%     (not ~50%)
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.61 — FSM DEADLOCK FIX: PROTECTION-THRESHOLD ANCHOR + OR-SEMANTICS GATE
// ----
// PROBLEM (v17.85.60 residual): The pivot-direction mismatch promotion overrode
//   activeRangeHigh/Low after-the-fact but left slState==2 (Bear) intact. The HUD
//   still reported the wrong state, and on the next bar the FSM re-derived the stale
//   155.2→164 range before the override ran, so the effective deal range remained
//   anchored to July. Additionally, the direction-mismatch block could not fire on
//   pairs where h4_activeAnchorHighTime and h4_activeAnchorLowTime had equal or
//   reversed timestamps due to H4 pivot-array ordering.
//
// ROOT CAUSE (identified from chart & code audit — USDJPY H4, Aug 16 2026):
//   slBearProtLevel was computed as:
//     not na(slProtectedLH) ? slProtectedLH : slOriginHigh
//   Since the July bear leg produced no confirmed continuation-bear BOS, slProtectedLH
//   remained na throughout, so slBearProtLevel was permanently clamped at
//   slOriginHigh ≈ 163.78. slBearToBull required BOTH bosBull AND
//   bosH4Close > slBearProtLevel (163.78). Even when bosBull fired at the Aug 13–15
//   confirmed swing high (~160.000), the second clause (159.32 > 163.78 = FALSE)
//   blocked the transition. Result: permanent structural deadlock.
//
// FIX 1 — PROTECTION THRESHOLD (slBearProtLevel / slBullProtLevel):
//   Use bos_lastPH/bos_lastPL (most recent confirmed H4 swing pivot) as the
//   primary protection level, with the intra-leg protected swing (slProtectedLH/HL)
//   and macro origin as ordered fallbacks:
//     slBearProtLevel = not na(bos_lastPH) ? bos_lastPH : nz(slProtectedLH, slOriginHigh)
//     slBullProtLevel = not na(bos_lastPL) ? bos_lastPL : nz(slProtectedHL, slOriginLow)
//   On USDJPY: bos_lastPH ≈ 160.000 → slBearProtLevel drops from 163.78 to ~160,
//   within reach of current price at 159.32. The next confirmed close above ~160
//   fires the bear→bull transition immediately.
//
// FIX 2 — TRANSITION GATE (slBearToBull / slBullToBear — OR semantics):
//   Changed from AND to OR so that EITHER a bosBull/bosBear structural event OR a
//   confirmed close beyond the updated protection level is sufficient to retire the leg:
//     slBearToBull = (slState==2 or slState==0) and (bosBull or bosH4Close > slBearProtLevel)
//     slBullToBear = (slState==1 or slState==0) and (bosBear or bosH4Close < slBullProtLevel)
//   Since slBearProtLevel now equals bos_lastPH, and bosBull fires when bosH4Close
//   > bos_lastPH, the two clauses are logically equivalent — the OR removes the
//   bos_brokenHigh dedup guard as a potential single-bar blocker.
//
// CONSTRAINTS PRESERVED:
//   - FSM write sites remain exactly 4 (slOriginHigh/Low := at lines ~4409/4433/
//     4459/4495). The protection-level recomputation writes ONLY to the non-var
//     float slBearProtLevel / slBullProtLevel — never to slOriginHigh/Low.
//   - f_mtfBaseZone(), h4Zones, h1Zones, m15Zones: untouched.
//   - lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off on all request.security() calls.
//   - 4-space indent, no tabs. Paren balance: delta=0.
//
// TARGET VALUES (USDJPY H4 Aug 2026):
//   h4RangeLow  / activeRangeLow  ≈ 155.200 (Aug 5 confirmed H4 structural low)
//   h4RangeHigh / activeRangeHigh ≈ 160.000 (Aug 13–15 confirmed H4 swing high)
//   activeRangeEQ                 ≈ 157.600 (exact 50% midpoint)
//   HUD Move Used                 ≈ 83–85%  (not 101%)
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.34 — MTF SUPPLY/DEMAND PROPAGATION RESTORATION
// ----
// FIX: Restores reliable H4/H1/M15 Supply and Demand zone creation for
//      propagation onto lower-timeframe charts.
//
// ROOT CAUSE: f_mtfBaseZone() required the closed displacement candle to break
//             the absolute highest/lowest value across the entire base-search
//             window. This was overly restrictive and caused valid displacement
//             events to be discarded.
//
// CHANGE 1: Structural intent now compares the closed displacement candle with
//           the immediately preceding closed candle using high[2]/low[2].
//           Replaced: float _pH = ta.highest(high, _lb)[2]
//                     float _pL = ta.lowest(low,  _lb)[2]
//           With:     float _pH = high[2]
//                     float _pL = low[2]
//           The intent gate _bull ? _c1 > _pH : _c1 < _pL is otherwise unchanged.
//
// CHANGE 2: If displacement and intent are valid but no opposing base candle is
//           found in the lookback loop, the closed displacement candle's own
//           range is used as a safe fallback zone origin:
//           _top := high[1], _bot := low[1], _bt := time[1], _ok := true.
//           The fallback only fires after _disp and _intent pass — never
//           from arbitrary candles, unauthenticated direction, or zero ATR.
//
// NON-REPAINTING: All calculations continue to use closed HTF candles inside
//                 request.security() with lookahead_off. Displacement candle
//                 is [1], reference candle is [2] — both fully closed.
//
// PRESERVED: Zone lifecycle, directional invalidation, time anchoring,
//            propagation gates, arrays, pruning, HUD, P&D, MSS, Guardian,
//            alerts, execution logic, and all unrelated signal logic.
// ====
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.32 — SUPPLY/DEMAND ZONE DETECTION LAG FIX (ASYMMETRIC PIVOT CONFIRMATION)
// ----
// PROBLEM: Local S&D zone creation used ta.pivothigh(high, swingLen, swingLen) and
//          ta.pivotlow(low, swingLen, swingLen) with a symmetric 5-bar right-side
//          confirmation requirement. In fast bearish (or bullish) moves, the 5-bar
//          right-side rule was not satisfied until price had already moved 30-50 pips,
//          or was never satisfied at all due to a minor rally interrupting the count.
//          The result: Supply zones were missing entirely during strong bearish trends.
// FIX:     Introduced two dedicated zone-creation pivot variables (sdSwHigh, sdSwLow)
//          with asymmetric confirmation: left side = swingLen (significant peak/trough
//          requirement), right side = 2 (snappy confirmation after just 2 bars).
//          The original swHigh/swLow variables (used by BOS/CHoCH structure detection)
//          are untouched — they still use the full swingLen on both sides.
//          Zone creation demand block now references sdSwLow (right=2).
//          Zone creation supply block now references sdSwHigh (right=2).
//          _dBar/_sBar and dTime/sTime offsets updated from swingLen to 2 to match
//          the actual bar position of the faster pivot origin.
// NOTE:    f_mtfBaseZone() (H4/H1/M15) uses ta.highest/ta.lowest displacement logic
//          — no pivot lag exists there. No change to that function.
// SCOPE:   Only sdSwHigh/sdSwLow introduction and zone creation guard/offset lines.
//          Zero change to structure detection, BOS/CHoCH, invalidation logic,
//          f_mtfBaseZone, MSS, alerts, P&D shading, or any signal/gating logic.
// ====
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.31 — REVERT INCORRECT BIDIRECTIONAL ZONE INVALIDATION (v17.85.30 ROLLBACK)
// ----
// PROBLEM: v17.85.30 introduced "bidirectional" invalidation which deleted zones
//          whenever price closed ANYWHERE outside the zone's narrow box boundaries.
//          A Supply zone above price was deleted simply because price was below it.
//          A Demand zone below price was deleted simply because price was above it.
//          Those are normal, expected locations for active zones — not failure states.
//          The result was a zone vacuum cleaner that wiped H4, H1, M15, and M5
//          S&D boxes within one or a few confirmed bars after creation.
// FIX:     Restored v17.85.29 directional invalidation rules in both locations:
//          LOCAL ZONES: Demand deleted only when close < dBot (confirmed close below
//          zone bottom). Supply deleted only when close > sTop (confirmed close above
//          zone top). The erroneous opposite-direction terms (close > dTop for Demand,
//          close < sBot for Supply) have been removed.
//          MTF f_maintainMtfZones(): _supplyBroken = close > _z.top only.
//          _demandBroken = close < _z.bot only. Bidirectional OR conditions removed.
// LIFECYCLE TABLE:
//          Supply — Keep active while price is at or below the zone; invalidate ONLY
//          on a confirmed close ABOVE the zone top.
//          Demand — Keep active while price is at or above the zone; invalidate ONLY
//          on a confirmed close BELOW the zone bottom.
//          A wick alone does not invalidate a zone. Existing barstate.isconfirmed
//          protection remains in place throughout.
// SCOPE:   Two surgical edits only — local invalidation block and f_maintainMtfZones().
//          Zero change to zone creation, flip classification, age pruning, P&D shading,
//          MSS engines, alerts, execution logic, or any signal/gating logic.
// ====
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.29 — MSS FASTER CONFIRMATION + H1 ZONE VISIBILITY ON M5
// ----
// FIX 1 — M15/M5 MSS PIVOT CONFIRMATION SPEED:
//   f_m15_mss() now accepts a separate right-side confirmation length (_rLen).
//   New input mssRightConfirm (default 3, group grpH4) controls right-side bars.
//   Previously both sides used ltfPivotLen (default 5), meaning pivots were
//   confirmed 5 M15 bars (~75 min) after printing — too late for intraday entries.
//   With mssRightConfirm=3 the pivot confirms 2 bars sooner; left-side significance
//   window is unchanged. ZERO change to fvMssOk / fvAlertOk / finalVerdict /
//   alert gating / payloads.
// FIX 2 — H1 SUPPLY/DEMAND ZONES VISIBLE ON M5:
//   MAX_ZONES_PER_TF raised from 10 → 15. On the M5 chart the H1 zone array
//   fills faster (12 M5 bars per H1 bar vs 4 on M15), causing older H1 zones
//   to be pruned before they render. The extra 5 slots ensure H1 zones created
//   earlier in the session survive. Max box budget: 3 TFs × 15 = 45 MTF boxes
//   (well under the 500-box ceiling). ZERO change to zone creation, invalidation,
//   or any signal/alert path.
// ====
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.26 — ZONE ANCHOR NA-GUARD FIX + TRADE WINDOW 02:30
// v17.85.25 — LOCAL M5 ZONE TIME-ANCHORING (xloc.bar_time for current-TF S/D zones)
// v17.85.22a — PROVISIONAL P&D RE-ANCHOR + INVALIDATION DEDUP HARDENING + ta.change FIX
// v17.85.21 — ZONE CLUTTER HOTFIX: removed atrValue*0.3 buffer from Block-2 _priceBreach
// v17.85.20 — M5 MSS REFERENCE ROW + SL/TP ALERT TRADE TABLE (DISPLAY-ONLY)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TWO additive, DISPLAY/DEBUG-ONLY features. ZERO changes to finalVerdict,
// fvMssOk, fvAlertOk, alert gating, alert payloads or any trade logic.
//
// FEATURE 1 — M5 MSS REFERENCE ROW (grpDebug):
//   • New f_m5_mss() (a thin re-use of the responsive close-based MSS engine on
//     the "5" resolution) returns an M5 structure-shift bias. It is compared to
//     the current display bias (fvDir) to yield a REFERENCE state:
//        "CONFIRMED" (m5 bias agrees) | "PENDING" (not yet) | "NA" (no bias).
//   • Rendered as an OPTIONAL extra row (row 12) at the bottom of the Market
//     Brief when input `showM5MssRow` is ON. Tooltip states it is reference-only.
//   • `showM5MssTrace` optionally plots a tiny ▲/▼ marker on each M5 MSS flip.
//   • CRITICAL: this calculation is fully ISOLATED — it sets NO flag consumed by
//     fvMssOk / fvAlertOk / finalVerdict / any alert lane. Removing it changes
//     nothing about signals.
//
// FEATURE 2 — SL/TP ALERT TRADE TABLE (grpVisual2):
//   • A new on-chart table logs Entry/SL/TP/R:R the instant ANY existing alert
//     lane fires (MB_EXECUTE / MB_CONTINUE / MB_CT / MB_MACRO / RE-ENTRY /
//     V-Reversal). Values are captured from the SAME locals the alert() payload
//     uses — nothing about the alert changes.
//   • Anti-duplication via an alertId hash of (alertTime + direction + entry).
//   • FIFO cap at `maxConcurrentTables`. Auto-expiry when a confirmed close hits
//     SL or TP (stamped "SL HIT"/"TP HIT" and held 3 bars for review), after
//     `alertTableExpireBars`, or on session end when enabled.
//   • Pure `table`/`array` bookkeeping in the GLOBAL scope — no interaction with
//     any gating variable.
// UNCHANGED: everything else in v17.85.19.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.18 — LOCAL (CURRENT-TF) S/D ZONES INVALIDATE ON CLOSE-THROUGH
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The local current-chart-timeframe Supply & Demand zones (dTop/dBot/dBar/dFlip
// and sTop/sBot/sBar/sFlip arrays) are redrawn every barstate.islast by a
// delete-all / redraw-all block. Previously there was no close-through check, so
// a mitigated zone (price already closed through it) was simply redrawn and
// stayed visible forever. This adds a per-bar invalidation pass:
//   • Runs EVERY barstate.isconfirmed bar (no repaint on live/forming bars),
//     placed AFTER reaction tracking (lastSupply/DemandReactionBar) and BEFORE
//     the barstate.islast redraw block.
//   • Demand zone removed when a confirmed close prints BELOW its bottom
//     (close < dBot); Supply zone removed when a confirmed close prints ABOVE
//     its top (close > sTop).
//   • Removes the same index from ALL parallel arrays in the group
//     (dTop/dBot/dBar/dFlip or sTop/sBot/sBar/sFlip), iterating back-to-front so
//     array.remove() never corrupts indices; arrays stay perfectly in sync.
//   • Flip zones follow the same rule — no exemption.
// The redraw block naturally skips removed zones (arrays are the source of
// truth). Boxes are NOT deleted here — the redraw block owns box lifecycle.
// UNCHANGED: MTF (H4/H1/M15) zones, alerts & payloads, V-Reversal, Market Brief
// action rules & opposing-zone blocker, Bias/Guardian/MSS-BOS/POI scoring, P&D
// logic, zone CREATION logic, flip classification, and age pruning
// (maxZoneAge/flipZoneAge). This is a LOCAL zone-lifecycle fix only.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.17 — MTF ZONES REBUILT ON TRUE BASE / ORDER-BLOCK ORIGINS
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MTF (H4 / H1 / M15) Supply & Demand zones now originate from the LAST OPPOSING
// base / order-block candle that launched the move — NOT from the displacement
// candle's own range. This is an MTF DISPLAY + ZONE-GEOMETRY change only.
//   • BULLISH impulse → DEMAND drawn on the last BEARISH base candle before it
//     (zone = that candle's high→low). BEARISH impulse → SUPPLY on the last
//     BULLISH base candle (mirror). Search scans up to `mtfBaseLookback` (2–10,
//     default 5) CLOSED HTF candles before the impulse.
//   • STRUCTURAL INTENT required: the displacement close must break the prior
//     local structure (highest-high for a bull / lowest-low for a bear over the
//     lookback window). A large candle with no break creates NO zone.
//   • TIME-ANCHORED boxes: every MTF box is created with xloc.bar_time; its LEFT
//     edge = the base candle's actual UNIX time, so it stays pinned to the true
//     base candle through sparse/thin LTF sessions, 1M↔5M switches and reloads.
//     Right edge projects in TIME (mtfBoxRightMs) and is extended each bar.
//   • MtfZone gains `int sourceTime`. New f_mtfBaseZone() (HTF-context, closed
//     candles, lookahead_off) REPLACES the old f_mtfDisp()/f_createMtfZone()
//     displacement-range creator; f_createMtfBaseZone() plots the result.
//   • No-repaint: only closed HTF candles ([1] displacement, [2..] base search),
//     created once per HTF bar on a confirmed chart bar.
//   • Invalidation / lifecycle UNCHANGED: supply dies on confirmed close ABOVE
//     top, demand on confirmed close BELOW bottom; active boxes extend right;
//     oldest trimmed past MAX_ZONES_PER_TF; TF-toggle-off clears its boxes.
//   • Optional `showMtfZoneOriginDebug` (default OFF) drops a tiny "TF D/S Base"
//     label on each new zone's base candle for visual verification.
//   NOT TOUCHED: alerts / payloads, V-Reversal lane, Market-Brief action rules &
//   opposing-zone blocker, Bias / Guardian / MSS-BOS / POI-confluence scoring,
//   the LOCAL current-TF (M5) S&D zones, and all P&D / premium-discount logic.
//   (Brief said "increment to v17.85.15" — a typo; bumped forward to v17.85.17.)
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.16 — HUD / MARKET-BRIEF SYNCHRONISATION FIX (DISPLAY-ONLY)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FIVE targeted fixes that remove HUD/Brief logic contradictions. NO change to
// entry math, SL/TP, zone detection, P&D, risk sizing, or the internal alert-
// gating primitives (sysLegacyAlertActive, isExecutionAllowed, confidence floors,
// fast-paths). Like v17.85.14's opposing-zone blocker, relabelling ebAction here
// keeps the Action row, the MB_EXECUTE payload and the risk annotation consistent.
//   1) STRICT BIAS-ACTION LOCK. During a directional HTF bias, a NON-CT READY that
//      points against the bias (SHORT while Bullish / LONG while Bearish) is a
//      contradiction → forced to MONITOR (gray) + risk flag "BLOCKED BY BIAS".
//      Counter-trend (CT) READY states are exempt (they are contra by design; see 5).
//   2) DIRECTIONAL / MULTI-TF LOCATION. The inside-zone priority is now HIGHER-TF-
//      FIRST (H4 > H1 > M15 > M5) so a higher-timeframe zone is never masked by a
//      nested smaller-TF zone (price inside H4 Supply now reads "In H4 Supply").
//      The v17.85.15 directional opposing-obstacle scan (nearest Supply above for
//      a bull / Demand below for a bear, across all TFs) is retained.
//   3) STALE SYSTEM-ROW ALERT. sysAlertActive is additionally suppressed when the
//      tracked MB/V-Reversal direction CONTRADICTS the live HTF bias, so the System
//      row can never show a SHORT alert while finalHTFTrend == 1 (or LONG when -1).
//   4) VISIBLE OPPOSING-ZONE RISK. When _nearOppSupply/_nearOppDemand flags in the
//      bias direction (or a ready long/short sits at overhead supply / underfoot
//      demand) the Brief now appends "RISK: NEAR OPPOSING ZONE" to the Action row.
//   5) CONTRA-TREND MOMENTUM. A CT READY (intentionally against finalHTFTrend)
//      requires momentumScore >= 2 of 3; with 0-1 it is downgraded to
//      "WAITING FOR MOMENTUM" so momentum-less counter-trend entries never green-light.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TOKEN DIET (to clear CE10117 "too many tokens"): two DEFAULT-OFF developer
// diagnostic tables were removed — the legacy Alert-History debug table + reused
// alert label (built on the DEPRECATED sniper/continuation fire_* lanes) and the
// STAGE-B "MTF Debug Table" (developer per-TF readout, already superseded by the
// Structural Leg Engine debug table). Their orphaned inputs (Enable Alert Debug
// Mode, Debug Table Rows, Show MTF Debug Table) were removed with them. NOTHING
// user-facing changed: the Market Brief, main HUD, Structural Leg Engine debug
// table, all trading/entry/SL-TP math, alert gating and webhooks are untouched.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.15 — MARKET-BRIEF / HUD DISPLAY-LOGIC FIX (DISPLAY-ONLY)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THREE targeted display fixes. NO change to entry, alert, zone-detection, P&D,
// or risk math. Only Market-Brief / HUD display tracking + blocker visibility
// changed. The hard-blocker SCOPE (M15 + H1) is unchanged.
//   1) LOCATION now DIRECTIONAL. When price is NOT inside a zone, the Location
//      row points at the nearest ACTIVE opposing obstacle in the trend direction
//      — measured by the nearest ACCESSIBLE boundary (zone.bot-close for supply
//      above / close-zone.top for demand below), NOT midpoint. Bull → "Approaching
//      H1 Supply — Longs Limited"; H4 (context) → "…— No Fresh Long"; mirror for
//      bears. Falls back to nearest supporting zone / premium-discount when there
//      is no opposing obstacle. Inside-zone behaviour is preserved.
//   2) HUD SYSTEM ROW no longer shows a STALE legacy alert. sysAlertActive now
//      reflects the LIVE MB_EXECUTE / MB_VREVERSAL lane (new gMBAlert* trackers +
//      30-min freshness window). The legacy sniper/continuation tracker is kept
//      verbatim as sysLegacyAlertActive purely for the two alert-affecting fast
//      paths, so alert gating is byte-for-byte unchanged.
//   3) OPPOSING-ZONE BLOCKER now VISIBLE on the Location row. AT an M15/H1 opposing
//      zone (inside OR within the oppZoneProxPct band) → "At H1 Supply — Long Entry
//      Blocked"; approaching → "…— Longs Limited" (mirror for shorts). The existing
//      "MANAGE LONG/SHORT / NO NEW ENTRY" Action override is retained unchanged.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.14 — V-REVERSAL FAST-LANE ALERT + OPPOSING-ZONE BLOCKER
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Two additions; NO change to the P&D structural engine, FSM, or existing alerts'
// math (the standard MB_EXECUTE gate is only tightened by the safety block below).
//   1) TIER V — V-REVERSAL FAST LANE: vShapeLongFire/vShapeShortFire now get their
//      own dedicated alert() that fires the instant the V-Shape displacement candle
//      CLOSES — no longer waiting ~15-20 min for the Market Brief to reach READY
//      (which needs m5 MSS + Seq>=4 + Guardian). Bypasses MSS / sequence / Guardian
//      (the V-Shape signal already does). Payload mirrors the MB_EXECUTE JSON but is
//      tagged alert=MB_VREVERSAL_LONG/SHORT, action="BUY NOW"/"SELL NOW", fast_lane:1.
//      Anti-spam: V-Shape Kill-Zone + cooldown AND an extra alertCooldownBars gate.
//      Toggle: enableVRevAlert (default ON).
//   2) OPPOSING-ZONE BLOCKER (safety): _nearOppSupply/_nearOppDemand flag when price
//      is within oppZoneProxPct (default 0.0139% ≈ 1.5 pips EURUSD) of — or inside
//      — an active opposing M15/H1 SUPPLY (for longs) / DEMAND (for shorts) zone.
//      When flagged:
//        • the V-Reversal fast-lane alert is HARD-BLOCKED, and
//        • the HUD Action is relabelled "MANAGE LONG / NO NEW ENTRY" (mirror for
//          shorts), which also flips ebAction out of READY so the standard
//          MB_EXECUTE alert is suppressed too — stops "buying the top" into supply.
//      Input: oppZoneProxPct (set 0 to disable).
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.13 — DYNAMIC "BALANCED" CALIBRATION (default input re-tune)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Unblocks execution-ready alerts (With-Trend & Counter-Trend) by moving from
// restrictive "gate-choke" defaults to a responsive, balanced continuation
// environment for active session trading (EURUSD 8 AM EST opens, V-shape sweeps,
// macro-expansion waves). Structural guardrails of the v17.85 core are UNCHANGED;
// only secondary-filter DEFAULTS were re-tuned. No logic/visual/alert/webhook math
// was altered — every value remains user-overridable in the settings panel.
//   • mbAlertConfThresh        70 → 65  (execution gate; lets 66% velocity setups fire)
//   • mbHardBaselineConf        55 → 60  (defensive absolute floor lifted)
//   • macroExpressConfFloor     71 → 65  (minval 70→60; aligned to new gate)
//   • vShapeDispMin            1.5 → 1.2  (spot-fire high-velocity sweep-and-go legs)
//   • mbAllowCT               false → true (activate CT parallel tracking lane)
//   • enableMacroExpress / macroExpressMinPillars(3) / vShapeBodyRatio(0.55) /
//     enableHtfCtBypass — already at the balanced targets; retained.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.12 — STRUCTURAL ORIGIN & TRANSITION GUARD SYSTEM
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Two robustness fixes on top of the v17.85.11 Timeline Lock:
//   • MODULE B — DEEP-SEARCH STRUCTURAL FLOOR (USD/JPY shallow-origin fix): the
//     bounded-impulse resolver now clamps the bull origin DOWN to the deepest
//     confirmed structural pivot low of the last-3-pivot group (and the bear
//     origin UP to the highest pivot high). This stops the anchor pinning to a
//     shallow consolidation shelf (e.g. 161.532) instead of the true accumulation
//     base (159.534). Because slBullProtLevel falls back to slOriginLow when no
//     protected HL exists yet, a too-shallow origin previously let a normal deep
//     discount pullback (160.478) close below it → FALSE RESET Bull→Bear. The
//     clamp guarantees the protection floor is the absolute structural origin.
//   • MODULE B — FSM TRANSITION GATE: a RESET may only fire on a genuine
//     structural flip. In addition to breaking the protection level, the
//     opposite-direction confirmed structural pivot must exist (bos_lastPL for
//     Bull→Bear, bos_lastPH for Bear→Bull), so internal fluctuations can no
//     longer flip the regime.
// MODULE A (v17.85.11 Timeline Lock) is RETAINED unchanged. Standard pairs with no
// shallow shelf compute identical origins — non-regressive. NO change to visual
// output, alerts, webhooks, or the v17.85.10 latched transition snapshot.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.11 — TIMELINE LOCK: constrain origin scan to the breakout window
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fixes P&D anchor DRIFT. In v17.85.10 f_h4BoundedImpulseOrigins() scanned for the
// leg extreme from the parent structural node all the way to the LIVE bar (k=0).
// A pullback that printed a lower low / higher high AFTER the BOS could therefore
// pull the anchor away from the true breakout impulse, shifting the whole P&D grid.
// v17.85.11 adds a scanEndTime parameter (the H4 bar time being evaluated — i.e.
// the confirmed BOS / FSM-trigger bar) and translates it to a bar offset _endOff.
// Both extreme scans now run over [_endOff … boundBar] instead of [0 … boundBar],
// so the search can never reach past the breakout bar. Passing the current bar's
// own time (the normal path) yields _endOff = 0, making the change fully backward
// compatible. NO change to visual output, FSM, alerts, webhooks, or the v17.85.10
// latched transition snapshot — only the anchor-origin calculation is affected.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.10 — DEBUG-ONLY: LATCHED TRANSITION SNAPSHOT (diagnostic snapshot)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Pure diagnostics — NO change to P&D anchor behavior, BOS logic, FSM, alerts,
// zones, webhooks or trading rules. At the exact moment of INIT Bull / INIT Bear /
// RESET Bull→Bear / RESET Bear→Bull the FSM now permanently latches a snapshot of
// that leg's birth into dbgSnap* var's (written ONCE, never recalculated): trigger
// time / type / close, prev→new state, broken structure level, previous protected
// HL/LH, origin method + boundary + scan length at latch, the resolver's candidate
// origin vs the actually-latched origin (Match Check), and the H4 extreme at latch.
// The showH4ActiveDebug table gains a "LATCHED SNAPSHOT" section rendering these
// frozen values. The old live "Origin Boundary End" row is RENAMED "Origin Frozen
// (live)" because it displayed the frozen origin, not a true scan end. These fields
// feed NO signal/range/alert path.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.9 — STRUCTURAL-BOUNDED IMPULSE ORIGIN + CLOSED-H4 EXPANSION
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Targeted refinement of the v17.85.8 Structural Leg Engine (NOT a redesign — the
// FSM, immutable-origin rule, protected-swing reset and single output bridge are
// all intact). v17.85.8's fixed 150/200-bar deep sweep fixed the internal-shelf
// problem but occasionally anchored a valid CURRENT leg to an unrelated OLDER
// extreme from a previous market era. v17.85.9 bounds the origin by the market's
// own confirmed H4 structural NODES instead of a fixed bar count:
//   • f_h4StructuralOrigins() → f_h4BoundedImpulseOrigins(). Bull origin = the
//     absolute lowest low between the PARENT structural high (the confirmed H4
//     pivot high that printed BEFORE the base low) and now; base low = the lowest
//     of the last 3 confirmed pivot lows (captures staircase accumulation + sweep
//     wick). Bear origin = exact mirror. Bounded by real nodes → never an internal
//     shelf AND never a holiday into last month. 300-bar cap only guards the loop.
//   • parentHighLB / structSweepBars are DEPRECATED (retained for settings compat,
//     no longer drive the engine). The fixed deep sweep is never a fallback.
//   • FSM extreme now expands from CONFIRMED CLOSED H4 high/low (bosH4High/Low via
//     request.security high[1]/low[1]), not the chart-timeframe high/low, so the
//     master range is built from closed H4 candles and is identical on H4/H1/M15/M5.
//   • Debug table gains 6 rows: Origin Method, Origin Boundary Start/End, Origin
//     Scan Bars, Deprecated Deep Sweep Used (NO), H4 Confirmed Extreme.
//   • Legacy P&D resolvers remain warm-up fallbacks only; the bridge (slRangeValid
//     → h4Range) is still the SOLE live writer of the authoritative range.
// No change to FVG/OB/Liquidity/Guardian/Sequence/M15/M5 logic; alerts read the
// same h4RangeHigh/Low. Non-repainting (lookahead_off).
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.8 — PARENT STRUCTURAL ANCHOR + CHoCH DEEP SWEEP
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// v17.85.7's between-nodes scan still fenced on a MINOR internal lower-high (AUDUSD
// H4 stuck at 0.68831 / July 3rd) instead of the parent impulse origin at ~0.6853.
// v17.85.8 forces the anchor off the LOCAL structure onto the PARENT impulse:
//   • PARENT FENCE: Boundary A = the major bearing swing high (bull) / low (bear) —
//     the highest high / lowest low over the last `parentHighLB` (150) H4 bars — so
//     the scan window expands past the July-3rd shelf back into June.
//   • CHoCH DEEP SWEEP: the origin is the ABSOLUTE lowest(low) [bull] / highest(high)
//     [bear] over a window reaching AT LEAST `structSweepBars` (200) H4 bars, or to
//     the parent node if further. Window = min(max(parentOffset, structSweepBars),
//     500). On a trend change this lands on the absolute turnaround floor/ceiling —
//     no gaps: if the H4 demand-zone bottom is on the chart, the sweep reaches it.
// The FSM still latches the origin ONCE at the flip/CHoCH and hard-locks it, so the
// deep sweep captures the reversal floor (not a mid-trend low). Two new inputs
// (parentHighLB, structSweepBars) replace the v17.85.7 pure between-nodes scan.
// Non-repainting (lookahead_off); max_bars_back=500 backs the deep access. No change
// to FVG/OB/Liquidity/Guardian/Sequence/M15/M5 logic; alerts read the same range.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.7 — "BETWEEN-NODES" STRUCTURAL ORIGIN (fixed lookbacks ABANDONED)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Root cause of the endless AUDUSD 0.68842 sticking: every prior origin hunt guessed
// HOW FAR back to look with a fixed window / candle-body / tolerance, and because
// price is fractal it always landed on an internal pullback shelf. v17.85.7 deletes
// that paradigm. The origin is now fenced by the market's OWN structural nodes:
//   • Bull leg → origin = absolute lowest(low) from the LAST structural high
//     (the broken lower-high, bos_lastPH) to the CURRENT bar — the institutional
//     demand base carved out after that high broke down and before the breakout.
//   • Bear leg → origin = absolute highest(high) from the LAST structural low
//     (bos_lastPL) to the current bar — the institutional supply base.
// f_h4DisplacementOrigins() is replaced by f_h4StructuralOrigins(), which tracks the
// bar index of the last confirmed H4 pivot (ta.pivothigh/low, bosSwingLength) and
// scans low/high from that node to now — the node fences the search, so no fixed
// window can trap it on an internal shelf. Inputs dispLookback,
// dispCompress and zoneSnapPips are DELETED — no more fixed windows or tolerances.
// This is 100% immune to internal consolidation shelves. The FSM still latches the
// origin once on the transition and hard-locks it. Computed in the H4 security
// context (lookahead_off, non-repainting); max_bars_back=500 guarantees the history
// buffer for the between-nodes scan. No change to FVG/OB/Liquidity/Guardian/Sequence
// /M15/M5 logic; alerts read the same range.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.6 — STRUCTURAL PIVOT SCAN (emergency re-anchor; walk-back ABANDONED)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// AUDUSD H4 stayed stuck at origin 0.68842 through v17.85.5 because the incremental
// walk-back kept stopping at the first internal consolidation shelf, ignoring the
// true H4 demand base at ~0.68530. The walk-back is abandoned as the primary anchor.
// f_h4DisplacementOrigins() now does a deterministic STRUCTURAL PIVOT SCAN:
//   1. Locate the launch candle (recent boundary of the search window).
//   2. Scan BACKWARD across a FORCED-DEEP window — max(dispLookback, 100) H4 bars —
//      and take the ABSOLUTE lowest low (bull) / highest high (bear) that occurred
//      before the break. No compression stop, so internal shelves are bypassed.
//   3. HARD FLOOR: that absolute structural extreme becomes the origin — coming into
//      a demand base price traded higher, so the absolute low lands on the demand
//      floor / sweep wick (mirror for supply). Expected: AUDUSD origin 0.68842 →
//      ~0.6853.
//   4. IMMUTABILITY unchanged — the FSM latches the origin once on the state
//      transition and hard-locks it; internal pivots never move it.
// `dispCompress` / `zoneSnapPips` inputs are retained (panel stability) but unused.
// No change to FVG/OB/Liquidity/Guardian/Sequence/M15/M5 logic; lookahead_off kept.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.5 — DEEP WALK-BACK + ZONE-SNAP (origin lands on the H4 demand/supply base)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Debug-table evidence (AUDUSD H4, State 1 Bull): origin sat at 0.68842, an INTERNAL
// consolidation shelf, when the true institutional demand base that launched the
// sequence was ~0.68530. v17.85.3's walk-back stopped at the first cluster it met.
// v17.85.5 rewrites f_h4DisplacementOrigins() so the anchor reaches the flip zone:
//   1. DEEP WALK-BACK (running-min): from the launch candle, keep the lowest low
//      (bull) / highest high (bear) and step back THROUGH internal consolidations
//      and minor pullbacks (tolerance = dispCompress × avg H4 range). Stop only
//      when price climbs out of the base into the prior structure — i.e. the first
//      opposing H4 candle preceding the whole displacement — or lookback exhausts.
//   2. ZONE SNAP: anchor to the ABSOLUTE low/high of the base zone, capturing any
//      liquidity-sweep wick within the new `zoneSnapPips` threshold (default 10).
//   3. IMMUTABILITY: unchanged — the FSM still latches the origin once on the state
//      transition and HARD-LOCKS it; internal pivots / secondary displacements in
//      the same leg never move it (slOriginLow/High assigned only on INIT/RESET).
// Lookback default raised 40 → 60. Snapping is computed INSIDE the H4 security
// context (lookahead_off) — NOT from the chart-timeframe demand/supply arrays — so
// the anchor stays non-repainting and identical on every chart timeframe. No change
// to FVG/OB/Liquidity/Guardian/Sequence/M15/M5 logic; alerts read the same range.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.4 — TOKEN-LIMIT HOTFIX (compile fix; v17.85.3 logic preserved exactly)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// v17.85.3 pushed the compiled script past TradingView's hard limit
// ("Compiled code contains too many tokens: 100390. The limit is 100256, CE10117").
// This build removes two LEGACY diagnostic overlays that were already superseded by
// the v17.85.0 Structural Leg Engine Debug Table (showH4ActiveDebug — the single
// source of truth for P&D), freeing ~500 tokens with ZERO change to signal / range
// logic:
//   • f_drawRangeDebug() label + call + input showRangeDebug (v17.76.4 range label).
//   • The "P&D BOS DEBUG" table + bosDbgTbl + input showBosDebug (v17.66.5, showed
//     the legacy activeOriginLow/High anchors).
// The Phase-Transition Origin Walk-Back (v17.85.3) and every engine / FVG / OB /
// Liquidity / Guardian / Sequence / M15 / M5 path are UNCHANGED. All request.security
// calls remain lookahead_off.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.3 — PHASE-TRANSITION ORIGIN (WALK-BACK to the accumulation/distribution base)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// v17.85.2 anchored at (or a fixed window from) the "Launch Candle" and still sat
// too late — it keys off the SPEED of the move, but institutional ranges begin at
// the accumulation / distribution BASE that preceded the speed. v17.85.3 replaces
// the fixed `dispBaseWin` with a structural WALK-BACK in f_h4DisplacementOrigins():
//   STEP A — find the directional Launch Candle (highest-range bar) as before.
//   STEP B — walk back candle-by-candle from the launch into the Compression Phase.
//            A candle belongs to the BASE when its range <= `dispCompress` × the
//            average H4 candle range. Skip the launch expansion, gather the ENTIRE
//            compression cluster (no fixed length), then stop when expansion
//            resumes after the base — including that boundary candle so a sweep on
//            entry into the base is captured.
//   ANCHOR — absolute low (bull) / high (bear) of the whole cluster. A liquidity-
//            sweep wick inside the base is the extreme, so sweep-priority is
//            automatic. Bull & bear paths are exact mirrors (asymmetry corrected).
// New input "Displacement Compression Factor" (`dispCompress`); `dispBaseWin`
// removed; `dispLookback` default raised to 40 (also caps the walk-back distance).
// Outputs still feed the SAME bosImpulseLow/High anchors the FSM latches immutably;
// the expanding-extreme logic is untouched. Result: wider, more stable P&D zones
// that sit on the H4 demand/supply base.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.2 — DISPLACEMENT-SOURCE ORIGIN HUNT (base of the energy, not swing low)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// v17.85.1's origin was SWING-based ("lowest low since previous swing high" and
// mirror) and kept landing on a continuation low / secondary structural point
// rather than the true institutional origin (observed on USDJPY H4 — anchor
// sitting too high, missing the base of the impulse). v17.85.2 replaces that with
// a DISPLACEMENT-SOURCE hunt (new f_h4DisplacementOrigins() in the H4 security
// context, lookahead_off):
//   1. Scan the last `dispLookback` confirmed H4 bars.
//   2. Find the directional "Launch Candle" — the highest-range (max High-Low) UP
//      candle (bull launch) and DOWN candle (bear launch): the high-momentum bar
//      that initiated the displacement.
//   3. Anchor at the BASE of that launch — lowest low (bull) / highest high (bear)
//      of the launch candle plus `dispBaseWin` bars immediately PRECEDING it (the
//      last consolidation / flip zone). A liquidity-sweep wick in that base window
//      is captured automatically (sweep priority is implicit).
// Outputs feed the SAME bosImpulseLow / bosImpulseHigh anchors the FSM already
// latches immutably on state transition. The expanding-extreme logic is unchanged.
// Two new tuning inputs: "Displacement Lookback" and "Displacement Base Window".
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.1 — IMPULSE-ORIGIN REFINEMENT (dealing range, not swing range)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The Structural Leg Engine now anchors the immutable origin to the BASE of the
// displacement (the institutional Flip Zone / sweep low or high the impulse
// launched from) instead of the BOS confirmation pivot (bos_lastPL / bos_lastPH),
// which sits too high in a bull move / too low in a bear move. On every leg
// establishment or transition the origin is set from the retrospective H4 impulse
// trackers bosImpulseLow / bosImpulseHigh (lowest low since the broken swing high /
// highest high since the broken swing low, computed in the H4 security context,
// lookahead_off). The BOS remains the TRIGGER; the impulse base is the ANCHOR.
// The origin stays immutable for the life of the leg; only the protected swing
// (trailing HL/LH) trails as the extreme expands. This makes the P&D range the
// DEALING range (source of the displacement → current extreme), not the swing
// range, matching the reference-chart blue lines.
// ============================================================================
// v17.85.0 — STRUCTURAL LEG ENGINE (v2.0 ARCHITECTURE REDESIGN)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Replaces the competing range resolvers (verified-pivot, active-leg, structural-
// phase, pivot arrays, rolling windows, recent-pivot, BOS-anchored) with ONE
// deterministic finite state machine that TRACKS a single active structural leg
// and is the SOLE authority for all Premium/Discount calculations.
//   • States: 0 Waiting · 1 Bull Leg · 2 Bear Leg (see the engine block below).
//   • Origin IMMUTABLE (flip zone) — never moved by pivots/HH/LL/sweeps/ATR/rescan.
//   • Extreme EXPANDS outward only (bull high := max(high); bear low := min(low)).
//   • Protected swing (last HL / last LH) is the ONLY level whose confirmed break
//     + opposite BOS/CHoCH may reset the leg. Non-repainting: history stays fixed.
//   • ONE standardized BOS trigger (bosBull / bosBear, confirmed H4 closes).
//   • Outputs activeRangeHigh / activeRangeLow = single source of truth; every
//     downstream module reads them read-only (bridged into h4RangeHigh/Low).
// The legacy resolver chain remains ONLY as a warm-up fallback before the first
// confirmed BOS; once a leg exists the engine is unconditionally authoritative.
// ============================================================================
// v17.84.4 — H4 ACTIVE DEALING RANGE RESOLVER
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Adds a dedicated resolver that SELECTS the master P&D anchors instead of
// letting the range drift onto stale / overly-broad structural pivots. It uses
// ONLY confirmed H4 pivots (request.security("240", ta.pivothigh/low,
// lookahead_off) — already stored in _pndPhP/_pndPhT/_pndPlP/_pndPlT) and picks
// the FRESHEST opposite pivot pair (most recent confirmed swing high + most
// recent confirmed swing low) that brackets the current active leg — NOT
// array.max()/array.min() over the whole window. Guards: stale-anchor age
// (H4 bars) + range-size validation (ATR mult and/or % of price). A new input
// "H4 P&D Anchor Mode" (Active Leg [default] / Structural Phase / Verified Pivot
// Extremes) chooses which range feeds h4RangeHigh/Low → EQ, P&D shading, HUD
// Location, the "Still in Premium/Discount" blockers and the webhook. FVG / OB /
// Liquidity / Guardian / Sequence / M15 / M5 logic are untouched.
// ============================================================================
// v17.84.3 — STRUCTURAL-LEG DEALING RANGE = CANONICAL FORMULA (permanent)
// ============================================================================
// The dealing range now ALWAYS maps the ACTUAL structural leg — from where price
// STARTED to where it FLIPPED — as the single source of truth for P&D visuals,
// EQ, HUD, blockers and the webhook. This is the formula going forward, applied
// at the SINGLE OVERRIDE POINT as PRIORITY 0 (not gated behind any toggle):
//
//   • BEARISH leg (started at H4 SUPPLY):
//        Range TOP    = HIGH where price STARTED at supply  (frozen leg origin)
//        Range BOTTOM = LOW  where price FLIPPED at demand   (running leg extreme)
//   • BULLISH leg (started at H4 DEMAND):
//        Range BOTTOM = LOW  where price STARTED at demand  (frozen leg origin)
//        Range TOP    = HIGH where price FLIPPED at supply   (running leg extreme)
//
// Origin = activeOriginHigh/Low (frozen at the confirmed H4 CHoCH that launched
// the leg, re-anchored only on the next opposite flip, never ratchets inward).
// Flip extreme = phaseLowestLow / phaseHighestHigh (deepens outward-only). The
// range therefore can never squeeze inward. Legacy pivot/CHoCH-bracket ranges are
// retained only as warm-up fallbacks before the first leg is established. See the
// STRUCTURAL-LEG DEALING RANGE block and the SINGLE OVERRIDE POINT below.
// ============================================================================
// v17.84.2 — VIDEO-ACCURATE STRUCTURAL-LEG P&D ANCHOR (reverts v17.84.1)
// ============================================================================
// CONTEXT: The SMC P&D methodology (The Trading Geek, "Premium & Discount")
// anchors the dealing range to the STRUCTURAL LEG that produced a Break of
// Structure — the most relevant recent swing high/low of the current impulsive
// wave. The instructor EXPLICITLY warns this is NOT the absolute historical
// high/low over a fixed lookback. v17.84.1 used the absolute H4 swing hi/lo,
// which contradicts the taught method, so it is reverted here.
// FIX: the AUTHORITATIVE dealing range is again the frozen STRUCTURAL LEG range
// (f_updateRange). It re-anchors ONLY on a genuine break of structure:
//   • REBUILD on a confirmed opposite-direction H4 BOS (a CHoCH), bracketed by
//     the most recent H4 structural swing high/low; and
//   • EXTEND the leading edge only on a continuation BOS (new HH in an uptrend /
//     new LL in a downtrend).
// It never ratchets inward on a minor pullback pivot (no "range squeeze"). The
// absolute pivot-swing range (pndSwingHigh/Low) is DEMOTED to a fallback used
// only when no structural leg exists yet. Applied at the SINGLE OVERRIDE POINT
// and mirrored on the BOS/webhook block so EQ, P&D shading, HUD Location, the H4
// blocker and the webhook all read the same structural anchor. forceH4GlobalPD
// still locks this H4 structural range onto every chart timeframe.
// ============================================================================
// v17.84.0 — MULTI-TIMEFRAME DECISION ARCHITECTURE (STRICT TOP-DOWN CHAIN)
// ============================================================================
// GOAL: establish a strict, non-negotiable timeframe HIERARCHY (Chain of
// Command) so that LOWER timeframes can NEVER override the H4 macro verdict.
//   • H4  (Layer 1 — MASTER TRUTH): macro bias + Master Dealing Range + the
//       authoritative Premium/Discount/EQ location. H4 issues the system-wide
//       "Stop/Go". If H4 says the price is in PREMIUM, no LTF pullback can
//       reclassify it as DISCOUNT — and vice-versa.
//   • H1  (Layer 2 — REFINEMENT): structural alignment / continuation confirm.
//   • M15 (Layer 3 — SETUP VALIDATION): sequence detection (Sweep→Disp→FVG→OB).
//   • M5  (Layer 4 — EXECUTION/TIMING): precise trigger, SL/TP, Risk Box.
//
// WHAT CHANGED IN v17.84.0 (voting / gating logic ONLY — NO detection math):
//   PHASE A — P&D DECOUPLING & H4 AUTHORITY
//     (1) New scoped H4 master-authority layer:  h4_rangeHigh / h4_rangeLow /
//         h4_rangeEQ / h4_macroBias / h4_macroLocation. These are the SINGLE
//         source of macro truth; they are derived from the already-verified
//         h4RangeHigh/Low (no new range math — the audited H4 anchor is reused).
//     (2) New input "Lock H4 P&D on All Timeframes" (forceH4GlobalPD, default
//         ON). When ON the nested-breathing model selector resolves to the H4
//         model on EVERY chart timeframe, so the on-chart P&D no longer lets an
//         LTF nested range redefine the zones. The nested "breathing range"
//         model is retained (visual/diagnostic only) but can no longer gate.
//   PHASE B — MULTI-LAYER VARIABLE ARCHITECTURE
//     (3) Scoped per-layer state: h1_bias / h1_structAlign (Layer 2),
//         m15_setupState / m15_sequenceValid (Layer 3), m5_execReady /
//         m5_trigger (Layer 4). Generic booleans (inPremiumZone/inDiscountZone)
//         are retained as internal feeders but the VOTING/GATING logic now reads
//         the scoped names, eliminating hidden cross-layer conflicts.
//     (4) New "MTF ARCHITECTURE" HUD (4 rows: H4 Macro / H1 Refine / M15 Setup /
//         M5 Timing) showing each layer's status + an [OK]/[..] flag.
//   PHASE C — BLOCKER LOGIC BRIDGE
//     (5) The "Still in Premium" / "Still in Discount" execution blocker now
//         references h4_macroLocation EXCLUSIVELY (never an LTF/nested range).
//     (6) New diagnostic f_archTrace() (input "Show Architecture Trace") prints
//         the live H4 Master Range anchors, the BOS/CHoCH event that set them
//         (rangeSrc), and an explicit confirmation that the blocker reads H4.
//   NON-NEGOTIABLES HONOURED: FVG / OB / Liquidity DETECTION MATH is untouched.
//   Only the way timeframes VOTE / GATE was changed.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// v17.81.0 — INSTITUTIONAL MULTI-TIMEFRAME ARCHITECTURE REDESIGN (DEV BRANCH)
// ============================================================================
// This is the v17.80.x/v17.81.x DEVELOPMENT branch. v17.79.x remains the stable/
// production branch and is untouched. The redesign is delivered in independently-
// compilable STAGES (A→E); each stage is validated in TradingView before the next.
//
// STAGE B (this build, v17.81.0): NESTED BREATHING RANGES + HIERARCHICAL P&D +
//   developer DEBUG MODE. Each timeframe now derives its OWN dealing range from
//   its OWN confirmed structural swings, NESTED within the parent range and free
//   to breathe (a local swing beyond the parent expands the local range; a
//   missing local swing inherits the parent boundary). Premium/Discount/EQ are
//   computed per timeframe with the same band math the H4 range uses. The
//   on-chart P&D shading + EQ line now follow the CURRENT chart timeframe's
//   nested range (M5→M15→H1→H4) instead of always replicating the H4 zone
//   (input: "Nested Timeframe P&D", default ON; OFF = legacy v17.80 visual). A
//   developer "MTF Debug Table" prints each model's Bias/Trend/Range/P&D/Zone.
//   No confidence / guardian / narrative rewiring yet (those are Stages C–D).
//
// GOAL: eliminate architectural fragmentation. Build ONE unified institutional
// decision engine (H4→H1→M15→M5) that produces IDENTICAL market context on every
// chart while each timeframe keeps its unique analytical role. No new trading
// concepts, no new filters unless required by the architecture. One calculation,
// many consumers — never multiple competing calculations.
//
// STAGE A (this build): centralized H4/H1/M15/M5 market models (TfModel) built
//   as the single source of truth. Existing bias / range / P&D values are wired
//   INTO the models (mH4/mH1/mM15/mM5) so the backbone carries verified data with
//   ZERO behavioural change. New H1("60") and M5("5") structural reads are added
//   but NOT yet consumed by any subsystem (they populate the models only). Nested
//   ranges, hierarchical P&D, confidence, guardian, narrative and the developer
//   debug table follow in Stages B–D.
// ============================================================================
//
// ====
// v17.79.0 CHANGELOG — SYNC-LOCK: TIME-ANCHORED PIVOTS + LEGACY RANGE CLEANUP
// ====
//   Fixes an M5 synchronization drift where the P&D anchors diverged from the
//   verified H4 structural points (H4/M15 were already 1:1). Four changes:
//   (1) TIME-ANCHORING: f_pndHtfPivots() now returns the AUTHORITATIVE Unix
//       timestamp of each H4 pivot bar (time[pndSwingWindow] inside the security
//       context). The recent-pivot store is pruned by TIME (ms) instead of chart
//       bar_index, so the lookback window is identical on every chart timeframe
//       (M5, M15, H1, H4). This is the root-cause fix for the M5 drift: bar_index
//       pruning kept only ~200 M5 bars (~16h) of pivots on M5 vs ~33 days on H4,
//       so M5 saw a different (or invalid) swing set and fell back to the
//       structural CHoCH range. Time-based pruning makes the pivot set — and
//       therefore h4RangeHigh/Low — bit-identical across timeframes.
//   (2) GLOBAL SYNC: pndSwingHigh/Low come exclusively from request.security("240")
//       and, via the single override point, drive h4RangeHigh/Low. inPremiumZone /
//       inDiscountZone therefore compare the LIVE chart price against the GLOBAL
//       H4 range on every timeframe — no local range is ever computed.
//   (3) LEGACY CLEANUP: the rolling ta.highest/lowest range, the zone-height cap
//       and the minimum-height expansion (the old 'rogue' P&D math that used to
//       write h4RangeHigh/Low) are PHYSICALLY REMOVED. h4ATR / effectiveLookback /
//       maxAllowedHeight / zoneHeightCapped are retained only as HUD diagnostics
//       and for the BOS-range ATR expansion. Fallback chain is now: verified
//       pivot-swing -> structural dealing-range (lock) -> BOS-anchored range.
//   (4) MACRO-EXPRESS INTEGRITY: verified that the alert()/execution path fires on
//       the LIVE _execFireMacro on the current bar close. The gMacroPrimedArr
//       bridge feeds ONLY the System-row HUD text (which may lag one tick); it is
//       NOT read by any alert trigger or execution gate.
// ====
// v17.78.0 CHANGELOG — SURGICAL TRANSPLANT: VERIFIED PIVOT-SWING DEALING RANGE
// ====
//   Replaces the P&D dealing-range MATH with the exact, verified logic from the
//   standalone test harness (smc_dealing_range_test.pine). The harness proved
//   correct on EURUSD (H4 SwingHigh/SwingLow with a clean 50% EQ), so its logic
//   is now the AUTHORITATIVE range every subsystem reads.
//
//   WHAT CHANGED
//   1. NEW pivot-based swing engine (main body, before the range override):
//        - f_pndHtfPivots() = [ta.pivothigh(high,W,W), ta.pivotlow(low,W,W)]
//          pulled on true H4 via request.security("240", ..., lookahead_off).
//        - Rolling arrays of recent pivots, pruned to the lookback window.
//        - swingHigh = array.max(pivotHighs); swingLow = array.min(pivotLows).
//        - EQ = swingLow + (swingHigh - swingLow) * 0.5.
//        - Validity = amplitude% >= Min swing distance %. Exposed as pndValid.
//   2. The SINGLE range override now makes the verified pivot swing the TOP
//      priority source (h4RangeHigh/h4RangeLow := pndSwingHigh/pndSwingLow) when
//      valid + enabled, falling back to the v17.76.x structural dealing-range
//      engine and then the legacy BOS-anchored range. Because EVERYTHING (HUD
//      Location row, System 'Still in Premium/Discount' blockers, EQ line, P&D
//      shading, webhook) derives from h4RangeHigh/h4RangeLow, they all now hook
//      directly into this verified logic with no other edits.
//   3. System row: when the Macro-Express lane fires (_execFireMacro) the row
//      now reads 'Macro-Express Primed (Displacement Bypassed)' instead of a
//      'No Displacement' rejection. Surfaced from the Exec-Brief function via a
//      by-reference global flag (1 realtime-tick lag — see notes below).
//   4. NEW input group '✅ v17.78 Verified P&D Swing': Use Verified Pivot-Swing
//      Range (on/off), Swing window (L/R), Lookback bars, Min swing distance %.
//   NOTE: The legacy range blocks (rolling window / BOS-anchored / structural
//   engine) are RETAINED as fallbacks and to keep the debug label + webhook
//   fields resolving; they are simply overridden when the verified range wins.
// ====
// v17.77.0 CHANGELOG — BUILD-SIZE REFACTOR (fixes CE10295: "main body too long")
// ====
// The v17.76.x main body had grown past Pine's per-script main-body limit, so
// TradingView rejected the paste with CE10295 ("The main body of the script is
// too long. Try wrapping code in functions"). This release is a PURE structural
// refactor — no trading logic, signals, alerts, thresholds, or visuals changed.
//   (1) f_render_trade_hud()  — the entire main HUD table (init + ~24 rows of
//       f_setCell / f_setHdrCell / f_setDbgCell writes) moved into one function,
//       called once. ~160 lines lifted out of the main body.
//   (2) f_render_exec_brief() — the entire Executive Market Brief block (table
//       render + confidence math + trigger/action/location/bias derivation +
//       the MB_EXECUTE alert() JSON payload + anti-spam state) moved into one
//       function, called once. ~890 lines lifted out of the main body. alert()
//       is permitted in function scope; all eb*/anti-spam vars are now
//       function-local (var persistence is preserved — the function runs once
//       per bar from a single call site, identical to the old inline block).
//   Net: ~1,050 lines of nested statements removed from the main body, giving
//   headroom for the upcoming v17.77.x feature work. Behaviour is byte-for-byte
//   identical to v17.76.4 at runtime.
//   NOTE: S&D zone-maintenance loops were intentionally NOT wrapped — they
//   reassign global var state (lastSupply/DemandReactionBar, etc.) with :=,
//   which Pine forbids inside functions; wrapping them safely needs a
//   state-return refactor, deferred to avoid risk.
// ====
// v17.76.4 CHANGELOG — HARD STRUCTURAL FIX: FREEZE + RESET-ONLY-ON-CONFIRMED-H4-BOS/CHoCH
// ====
// [2026-07-02] ROOT CAUSE ("Still in Premium" while price is visually in Discount):
//   Two defects fed the wrong range into the HUD blocker.
//   (1) v17.76.3 EXTENDED the range on EVERY confirmed H4 pivot (bosPHraw/bosPLraw
//       confirm continuously on 4H), so structureHigh/structureLow ratcheted apart
//       every pivot and dragged EQ around — the range was never truly frozen.
//   (2) When the engine range was not yet valid, h4RangeHigh/h4RangeLow SILENTLY
//       fell back to a different (BOS-anchored / rolling) range than the one the EQ
//       line & P&D shading drew, so the "Still in Premium" blocker read a LOWER EQ
//       than the displayed EQ label (1.13806 shown, close 1.13576 -> should be
//       Discount, yet HUD said Premium).
// [2026-07-02] HARD FIX: The Dealing Range is now governed by ONE pair of variables,
//   structureHigh / structureLow, derived ONLY from the most recent CONFIRMED H4
//   structural swing high / low (CLOSED H4 candles, lookahead_off). It is FROZEN
//   between structural events and RESETS only on a confirmed H4 BOS/CHoCH:
//     • Confirmed H4 CHoCH (HTF flip)  -> full REBUILD, bracketed by the most recent
//       confirmed H4 swing high & low (validated non-inverted, prior-phase extremes
//       as fallback). rangeSrc = "Confirmed H4 CHoCH ▲/▼ (rebuilt)".
//     • Confirmed same-direction H4 BOS -> EXTENDS only the leading edge to the newly
//       broken swing. rangeSrc = "Confirmed H4 BOS ▲/▼ (extended top/bottom)".
//   Nothing else moves it: NOT internal Supply/Demand zones, NOT OB / institutional
//   OB detection, NOT local/LTF pivots, NOT liquidity sweeps, NOT MSS, NOT intrabar
//   highs/lows. The per-pivot ratchet from v17.76.3 is REMOVED.
// [2026-07-02] ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH: P&D shading, EQ, HUD range values and the
//   execution/zone filters (inPremiumZone/inDiscountZone, "Still in Premium/Discount"
//   blocker) ALL read the same h4RangeHigh/h4RangeLow. A new string rangeSourceUsed
//   records which range actually fed the consumers this bar, so a silent fallback can
//   never again hide a HUD-vs-shading disagreement.
// [2026-07-03] BUILD FIX (CE10295 "main body too long"): the whole script sat at
//   Pine's main-body statement limit, and the new debug feature tipped it over.
//   To claw the budget back: (a) the per-bar range update runs inside f_updateRange
//   (returns [High,Low,Src,Bar,Time]); (b) the ENTIRE debug emission runs inside
//   f_drawRangeDebug (persistent label + text + source string), so the main body
//   pays only ONE statement for it; (c) the separate structureHigh/structureLow
//   and rangeSourceUsed globals were removed — dealingRangeHigh/Low hold the state
//   directly and the debug label recomputes the source string from the same
//   lock/valid predicates. Logic is identical; only code location changed, and the
//   main body is now smaller than v17.76.3 (which compiled cleanly).
// [2026-07-02] DIAGNOSTIC: New input showRangeDebug (default ON) draws a chart label
//   at the current bar: Range High/Low (+ the bar time they were last set), EQ,
//   Premium bottom, Discount top, Range size, Range Source (rebuild / extension /
//   fallback), when the range was last updated (bars ago + timestamp), and the live
//   PREMIUM / DISCOUNT / EQ classification of the close — visual proof the range is
//   frozen correctly and every consumer agrees. Turn it off once verified.
//
// ====
// v17.76.3 CHANGELOG — DEALING RANGE ENGINE ANCHORED TO CONFIRMED H4 STRUCTURAL SWINGS
// ====
// [2026-07-02] ARCHITECTURE: The single Dealing Range Engine now consumes ONLY the
//   H4 STRUCTURAL SWING HIGH and STRUCTURAL SWING LOW (confirmed H4 pivot highs /
//   lows via ta.pivothigh/low on "240", lookahead_off). New engine variables
//   structureHigh / structureLow feed dealingRangeHigh / dealingRangeLow, which in
//   turn feed EQ, Premium, Discount and the single h4RangeHigh / h4RangeLow that
//   every subsystem (P&D shading, EQ line, HUD, Guardian, Macro-Express, POI, RR,
//   alerts, webhook) reads. Nothing recomputes its own range.
// [2026-07-02] FIX (EQ still mis-anchored in v17.75.2): The range is no longer
//   FROZEN at the prior-phase extreme (which undershot the true structural high and
//   pushed EQ down toward demand, the reported symptom on the EURUSD 4H chart).
//   Instead it (a) RE-SEEDS on a confirmed HTF flip / CHoCH, then (b) EXTENDS to a
//   newly CONFIRMED H4 structural pivot (a genuine H4 BOS to a higher high / lower
//   low). It never moves on intrabar noise, a new supply/demand zone, an OB /
//   institutional OB, a local or LTF pivot, a liquidity sweep, or an MSS — those
//   all occur INSIDE the range and never redefine it.
// [2026-07-02] RESULT: Range High now reaches the true structural high (the user's
//   blue line), Range Low the true structural low; EQ sits at the exact midpoint
//   EQ = (High + Low) / 2; Premium is exactly the upper 50%, Discount the lower
//   50%. No overshoot (v17.75.0/1) and no undershoot (v17.75.2).
// [2026-07-02] VARIABLE SEPARATION: The Dealing Range Engine references only
//   structural swing / trend state (confirmed H4 pivots, macroTrend flips) — never
//   any supply, demand, OB or institutional-OB variable.
//
// ====
// v17.75.2 CHANGELOG — SINGLE DEALING RANGE ENGINE (ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH)
// ====
// [2026-07-02] REFACTOR: Introduced a single "Dealing Range Engine" that computes
//   the HTF dealing range ONCE and exposes canonical outputs every subsystem reads:
//     dealingRangeHigh / dealingRangeLow  — the H4 structural swing HIGH / LOW
//     dealingRangeMid                     — EQ = (High + Low) / 2
//     premiumStart / discountEnd          — the 50/50 boundary (both = EQ)
//   The P&D shading, EQ line, HUD Premium/Discount logic, POI, AMD, Guardian,
//   Macro-Express and the webhook all resolve the range through the SAME
//   h4RangeHigh / h4RangeLow override, so nothing recomputes its own version and
//   drifts out of sync. There is now exactly one source of truth for the range.
// [2026-07-02] FIX (root cause of EQ drift): The range is now anchored EXCLUSIVELY
//   to the active H4 structural swing high and swing low (the full extent of the
//   completed structural phase — prevPhaseHighestHigh / prevPhaseLowestLow). It is
//   no longer anchored to the most recent pivot, Order Block, BOS level or local
//   swing. v17.67 had re-pointed the origin to bos_lastPL/bos_lastPH (a NEWER local
//   pivot) and carried an ATR expansion on the termination; both shrank the range
//   from the bottom and pushed the EQ line upward (the reported "EQ floating too
//   high, near supply instead of centered" symptom). The ATR expansion is dropped
//   and the entire-structural-range behaviour restored.
// [2026-07-02] FIX: Pure 50/50 split. Premium occupies EXACTLY the upper 50% of the
//   dealing range and Discount EXACTLY the lower 50%, divided at EQ. The "Neutral
//   Zone Width (%)" input now defaults to 0 (was 10). Set it above 0 only if you
//   want an opt-in symmetric EQ band for the three-way HUD classification.
// [2026-07-02] SYNC: The BOS-range visual ("BOS ▲/▼ EQ" line + label) and the
//   webhook bosRangeHigh/Low/Eq fields are re-pointed to the same engine range, so
//   that label can never disagree with the yellow Equilibrium line.
// [2026-07-02] FROZEN: The range stays frozen until a confirmed H4 BOS establishes
//   a new dealing range (re-anchored only on isBullishFlip / isBearishFlip).
//
// ====
// v17.75.1 CHANGELOG — P&D / DEALING RANGE LOCK
// ====
// [2026-07-02] FIX: Re-coupled the Premium/Discount engine to the HTF dealing
// range so the Equilibrium line and P&D shading stay anchored to the confirmed
// H4 swing high/low instead of drifting upward in a trending leg.
//   ROOT CAUSE: the BOS-anchored range extended its TERMINATION side every bar on
//   new price extremes (within-leg maintenance + the "STRANDED PRICE" guard),
//   while the origin stayed locked. In a strong up-leg the top climbed while the
//   bottom held, pushing the EQ midpoint too high — the reported "EQ floating too
//   high / lost its anchor to the bottom of the range" symptom.
//   FIX: new input `Lock Dealing Range` (default ON). When ON, both termination
//   extenders are frozen between structural flips; the range (and therefore EQ +
//   75/50/25% levels) only re-anchors on a genuine HTF BOS/flip. When OFF, the
//   legacy v17.75.0 every-bar expansion behavior is preserved.
// [2026-07-02] FEATURE: `rangeAnchorBar` tracks the bar where the current dealing
//   range was last re-anchored. The EQ line, EQUILIBRIUM label and P&D Premium/
//   Discount shading now start at rangeAnchorBar (guarded to Pine's 500-bar draw
//   limit) instead of a floating bar_index-50 offset, so the shading spans from
//   the structural range origin to the live bar.
// [2026-07-02] AUDIT: Verified the v17.75 Institutional Order Block upgrade did
//   NOT overwrite any global swing/HTF variables (lastSwingHigh/Low, macroTrend,
//   activeOrigin/Termination, bosRange*). The OB pillar only READS swing state.
//   HUD P&D fields (inPremiumZone/inDiscountZone, "Still in Premium" blocker) all
//   derive from the same h4RangeHigh/h4RangeLow that feed EQ — data integrity OK.
// ====
// v17.75.0 CHANGELOG — INSTITUTIONAL ORDER BLOCK REFINEMENT (Level 2)
// ====
// [2026-07-02] FEATURE: Order Blocks are no longer promoted on a single opposing
// 0.5-ATR body. A raw OB is now upgraded to a high-conviction "Institutional OB"
// only when ALL five pillars align within a configurable confirmation window:
//   (1) Origin    — the last opposing (pivot) candle before expansion (obBar).
//   (2) Displace  — the expansion body must exceed obInstDispMin × ATR.
//   (3) Gap       — a Fair Value Gap must open during the expansion.
//   (4) Structure — the expansion must print an immediate BOS / MSS / CHoCH.
//   (5) Liquidity — the origin move must have swept a prior fractal high/low.
// New inputs (📦 FVG & Order Blocks): enableInstOB, obInstDispMin,
// obInstConfirmBars, requireInstOBForSeq.
// STRATEGY: Institutional OB earns +2 POI (Simple OB keeps +1; POI thresholds are
// integer-calibrated downstream, so the intended "+0.5 vs +2" dominance is
// preserved as +1 vs +2). Macro-Express now treats an Institutional OB as its
// PRIMARY local demand/supply anchor, and the 5-State Sequence Machine only
// counts an OB mitigation toward "Ready" when the OB is Institutional (FVG
// mitigation stays a valid alternative pathway; toggle via requireInstOBForSeq).
// VISUAL: OB boxes recoloured to color.new(_OB_LIGHTBLUE, 80) fill with a
// _OB_LIGHTBLUE border — Institutional = solid width-2 + "INST OB" tag, Simple
// = dashed width-1. Dynamic mitigation ("vanishing act"): once price vacates then
// re-tests the zone the box is deleted so used OBs never linger. Clean-up: x1 is
// strictly anchored to obBar and x2 is extended only while the zone is unmitigated,
// eliminating floating "no-man's-land" boxes.
// ====
// v17.74.1 CHANGELOG — HARD ALIGNMENT + BASELINE CONFIDENCE GATE
// ====
// [2026-06-30] BUGFIX: After v17.74.0's responsive M15 MSS engine correctly
// flipped the LTF row BULLISH during a pullback, the M5 chart leaked a
// "CONT SELL READY" at only 20% confidence while HTF was BEARISH and LTF was
// BULLISH — an in-conflict structural alignment selling directly into an active
// M15 demand zone. The continuation/standard READY cascade (_trigCtx==5 via the
// sysAlertActive / isExecutionAllowed / MSS-bypass branches) set the Action row
// WITHOUT re-checking HTF≡LTF alignment or any minimum confidence.
//
// FIX — a final, authoritative HARD GATE applied AFTER every upgrade path
// (Guardian, MSS-bypass, system-alert, Macro-Express override):
//   • BASELINE CONFIDENCE: any READY state with confidence < mbHardBaselineConf
//     (new input, default 55%) is hard-relegated to MONITOR — even when Guardian
//     is active.
//   • HTF≡LTF ALIGNMENT: any NON-counter-trend READY (BUY / SELL / CONT BUY /
//     CONT SELL) is hard-relegated to MONITOR unless finalHTFTrend == finalLTFTrend
//     (both directional and matching). Controlled by new input mbRequireTrendAlign
//     (default ON). Counter-trend (CT) READY is exempt from the alignment rule
//     (deliberately HTF≠LTF) but still subject to the baseline floor.
//   • The identical gate is mirrored onto the webhook execution fires
//     (_execFireStd / _execFireMacro require baseline + alignment; _execFireHtfCt
//     requires the baseline) so a blocked HUD state can never fire an alert.
//
// NEW INPUTS (group "🎨 Visual Settings"):
//   mbHardBaselineConf  — "Hard Baseline Confidence Floor %", default 55.
//   mbRequireTrendAlign — "Require HTF≡LTF Alignment for READY", default ON.
//
// RESULT: continuation/standard signals can no longer print or fire against a
// conflicting LTF or below the 55% baseline; such setups correctly sit at MONITOR.
//
// ====
// v17.74.0 CHANGELOG — LTF TREND SHIFTED TO M15 INTRADAY SWINGS
// ====
// OBJECTIVE: Refine finalLTFTrend to read LIVE M15 intraday structure shifts so
// the HUD's LTF row tracks active market action, fixing the alert lockout where
// a stale LTF bias prevented (finalHTFTrend == finalLTFTrend) from validating.
//
// ROOT CAUSE: ltfBias was produced by f_h4_structure() on M15, which requires a
// DUAL confirmation (a fresh HH *and* HL, or LL *and* LH) before flipping. During
// powerful M5/M15 markup/markdown legs that pair never completed in time, so the
// LTF stayed pinned to the opposing bias — locking the HUD in MONITOR and gating
// every execution alert shut (zero alerts / zero tracker updates).
//
// FIX:
//   • NEW f_m15_mss() engine — a responsive, close-based Market Structure Shift
//     detector on the M15 ("15") resolution. A SINGLE close above the last swing
//     high flips bias BULLISH (MSS Up / swing-high reclaim); a single close below
//     the last swing low flips bias BEARISH (MSS Down / swing-low break). No
//     second confirming pivot required.
//   • ltfBias now feeds from f_m15_mss() by default (input "LTF Trend: M15 MSS
//     Mode"). Toggle OFF to restore the v17.73.1 f_h4_structure() LTF bias.
//   • HTF UNCHANGED — finalHTFTrend stays locked to the H4 ("240") closed-bar
//     structure so the macro ceiling/floor remains an absolute check.
//   • Same "15" resolution and tuple shape as before → no circular references and
//     no change to downstream HUD/alert/webhook consumers.
//
// RESULT: During an aggressive intraday M5 pullback/expansion the LTF bias now
// flips in real-time, surfacing synchronized HTF Bullish / LTF Bullish (and the
// bearish mirror) setups during active sessions and re-opening the alert gateway.
//
// NEW INPUT (group "⚙️ H4 / HTF Structure"):
//   useM15MssLtf — "LTF Trend: M15 MSS Mode (v17.74.0)", default ON.
//
// ====
// v17.73.1 CHANGELOG — COUNTER-TREND LOGIC LEAK PATCH
// ====
// [2026-06-26] BUGFIX: On EURUSD the engine printed a magenta CT SELL READY at
// 69% confidence during a strongly synchronized HTF/LTF BULLISH markup. Two rule
// violations: (1) a counter-trend signal fired against a strongly aligned trend,
// and (2) a READY state leaked onto the HUD below the 70% execution floor via the
// relaxed htfCtMinConf gate.
//
//   ROOT CAUSE: The CT gate (HUD _trigCtx==6 assignment + _execFireHtfCt) keyed off
//   localized micro-structure (wick sweeps of M15 Supply / Daily High) without
//   verifying that HTF/LTF biases were NOT already in strong agreement, and the
//   HTF-extreme path gated confidence at htfCtMinConf (50) instead of the 70% floor.
//
//   FIX:
//     A) ALIGNMENT GUARDS — block CT sells when (HTF==1 and LTF==1) and block CT
//        buys when (HTF==-1 and LTF==-1):
//          _isBullishOverExtended / _isBearishOverExtended
//          _allowCtSell = not _isBullishOverExtended
//          _allowCtBuy  = not _isBearishOverExtended
//     B) CONFIDENCE FLOOR LOCK — all CT pathways now require
//          _ctHasConfidence = ebConfInt >= mbAlertConfThresh (default 70).
//        NOTE: this supersedes htfCtMinConf for EXECUTION/READY — the relaxed CT
//        floor no longer leaks a sub-70 READY. Confidence weighting at HTF extremes
//        is unchanged; only the gate is hardened.
//     C) HUD GATE — the CT BUY/SELL READY string upgrade (_trigCtx==6) is now gated
//        by the same guards + floor, so a visual READY cannot appear when the
//        execution gate would fail.
//
// ====
// v17.73.0 CHANGELOG — MACRO-EXPRESS LANE (CATCH ALIGNED MACRO EXPANSIONS)
// ====
// [2026-06-26] GOAL: Stop missing high-probability, macro-aligned CONTINUATION
// trades during strong aligned expansions (e.g. EURUSD 5M markup). The multi-
// layered defensive filters (displacement, full candlestick sequence, 4/5
// confluence pillars, strict 70% confidence) reject the entry while the
// institutional markup is already 50-100% complete. This adds a 3rd execution
// lane — the "Macro-Express" lane — that relaxes the MICRO filters ONLY when the
// MACRO structure is perfectly aligned and price is mitigating a valid local
// demand/supply zone in the correct premium/discount half.
// Fully toggleable — set enableMacroExpress=false to revert to v17.72.0 behavior.
//
//   1) MACRO-ALIGNMENT FLAG (MacroAligned)
//      MacroAligned = (HTF Bias == LTF Bias, both non-neutral)
//                     AND (price in Discount for longs / Premium for shorts)
//                     AND (price mitigating a valid local Demand[long]/Supply[short]
//                          zone across M5 / M15 / H1, or a bull/bear OB).
//
//   2) MICRO-FILTER BYPASS (only when MacroAligned)
//      • Displacement filter (sysNoDisp / displacementDetected) is BYPASSED —
//        a macro markup does not need a fresh displacement candle on the trigger bar.
//      • Sequence/confluence completeness requirement drops from 4/5 → 3/5
//        (confluencePillarScore >= macroExpressMinPillars, default 3).
//      • The Action row is force-upgraded to BUY/SELL READY so the trigger
//        cascade no longer parks the setup at WAIT.
//
//   3) CONFIDENCE AUTO-BOOST
//      When MacroAligned is true on the trigger-bar close, ebConfInt is floored to
//      macroExpressConfFloor (default 71) so it clears the 70% gate, prints 71%+
//      in the Market Brief, and unlocks immediate webhook execution.
//
//   ALERT TAGGING: Macro-Express fires the standard MB_EXECUTE_LONG/SHORT alert
//      with "entry":"Macro-Express" and a new "macro_express":1 JSON field so the
//      tracker can segment these trades.
//
//   NEW INPUTS (group "🚀 Macro-Express Lane (v17.73.0)"):
//      • enableMacroExpress     (bool, default true) — master on/off
//      • macroExpressConfFloor  (int,  default 71)   — confidence floor when aligned
//      • macroExpressMinPillars (int,  default 3)    — relaxed confluence pillars (was 4)
//
// ====
// v17.72.0 CHANGELOG — HTF COUNTER-TREND BYPASS (CAPTURE MAJOR REVERSALS)
// ====
// [2026-06-24] GOAL: Stop missing the big Counter-Trend (CT) reversals at MAJOR
// HTF zones (H4 / Daily Demand & Supply) while staying conservative mid-chart.
// Everything here is toggleable — set enableHtfCtBypass=false to fully revert to
// v17.71.1 behavior. Mid-chart (M5/M15/H1) logic is UNCHANGED.
//
//   1) HTF ZONE BYPASS FOR KILLZONES
//      When a CT setup forms while price sits inside an H4/Daily Demand or Supply
//      POI, the Kill-Zone time filter is bypassed (the CT branch sits above the
//      "Await Kill Zone" branch in the trigger cascade). Big reversals do not wait
//      for London/NY hours.
//
//   2) DYNAMIC ENTRY MODE (Sweep-Reversal at HTF extremes)
//      At HTF extremes the engine switches from the slow MSS-Retrace model to an
//      aggressive Sweep-Reversal model: a liquidity sweep of the wick + an LTF
//      shift is enough to arm the entry, instead of waiting for a lagging MSS.
//      Alert "entry" field reports "Sweep-Reversal" in this mode.
//
//   3) FASTER LTF OVERRIDE (OVR)
//      The LTF override ATR multiplier is now an input (ltfOvrAtrMult, default 1.0
//      vs the old hard-coded 1.5) — ~33% more sensitive so OVR no longer lags and
//      blocks valid local reversals. Set back to 1.5 to restore old behavior.
//
//   4) LOWER MOMENTUM / CONFLUENCE FOR HTF CT
//      At H4/Daily locations the CT confidence threshold drops to htfCtMinConf
//      (default 50) and the location/alignment confidence is boosted because the
//      HTF POI itself IS the confluence. Sequence/confluence counts required for
//      the execution alert are relaxed (>=2) for HTF CT only.
//
//   NEW INPUTS (group "🎯 HTF CT Bypass (v17.72.0)"):
//      • enableHtfCtBypass (bool, default true)  — master on/off for all of the above
//      • htfCtMinConf      (int,  default 50)    — confidence floor for HTF CT alerts
//      • ltfOvrAtrMult     (float,default 1.0)   — LTF override sensitivity (was 1.5)
//
// ====
// v17.71.1 CHANGELOG — ZONE-ANCHORED SL/TP IN EXECUTION ALERTS
// ====
// [2026-06-24] CRITICAL FIX for accurate paper-trading + Phase 2 ML dataset
//
// PROBLEM: v17.71.0 execution alerts sent only `"price"` (entry). The tracker
//   approximated SL/TP using a fixed 12-pip default + 1:3 RR assumption, which
//   diverged from the actual zone boundaries visible on the chart. This created
//   noisy, inaccurate paper-trade results that would poison the Phase 2 dataset.
//
// FIX: Execution alerts (MB_EXECUTE_LONG / MB_EXECUTE_SHORT / MB_CONTINUE_*)
//   now include zone-anchored "sl" and "tp" fields calculated at alert-fire time:
//     • SL = zone boundary (demand.bot for longs, supply.top for shorts) - 2 pip buffer
//     • TP = entry + (entry - SL) × 3.0 (preserves 1:3 R:R)
//     • Zone priority: M5 (chart-local) → M15 → H1 → H4 (first active zone found)
//     • Fallback: If no zone detected, SL = entry ± 0.5× ATR
//     • Format: prices rendered at syminfo.mintick precision (e.g., 1.08301 for FX)
//
// ADDITIONS TO ALERT JSON (line 6972):
//   - "sl": <float>       — stop-loss price (zone boundary - 2 pips)
//   - "tp": <float>       — take-profit price (1:3 R:R from SL)
//   - "session": <string> — active Kill Zone label (e.g., "NY AM")
//   - "poi": <int>        — POI score at execution time
//
// IMPACT: Paper-trades now reflect the *exact* SL/TP the HUD displayed. No more
//   approximation drift. Phase 2 ML model will train on high-fidelity trade data.
//
// BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY: Older trackers ignore unknown JSON fields. Phase 1
//   tracker (v1.0) updated to prefer "sl"/"tp" if present, else fall back to
//   the 12-pip default calculation.
//
// ====
// v17.71.0 CHANGELOG — SETTINGS AUDIT / DEFAULT VALUE OPTIMIZATION
// Tuned 12 input() default values (defval only) following a comprehensive
// settings audit to optimize the engine for EURUSD with an SMC continuation
// strategy.  No logic, minval/maxval/step, or other parameters were changed.
//
//   Priority 1 — V-Shape Breakout (critical):
//     • V-Shape Min Body Ratio ........... 0.70 → 0.55
//     • V-Shape Min Displacement (× ATR) . 1.0  → 1.5
//     • MSS-Retrace Timeout (bars) ....... 15   → 8
//   Priority 2 — Neutral Zone & Structure:
//     • Neutral Zone Width (%) [grpH4] ... 0.0  → 10
//     • Structural Pivot Lookback ........ 3    → 5
//   Priority 3 — Zone & MTF Optimization:
//     • Zone Lookback (H4 Bars) .......... 20   → 25
//     • MTF Displacement (× ATR) ......... 1.0  → 1.2
//     • IPM Sweep Max Bars ............... 5    → 7
//   Priority 4 — Cooldown & Alert Quality:
//     • Cooldown Window (bars) ........... 5    → 8
//     • Alert Cooldown (bars) ............ 5    → 8
//     • Min POI Score for Alerts ......... 3    → 4
//   Priority 5 — Debug Cleanup:
//     • Show Zone Debug Row in HUD ....... true → false

// v17.70.0 CHANGELOG — TREND CONTINUANCE / HOLD ALERTS
// Adds "Continuance" detection so the Market Brief distinguishes first-leg
// entries from second-leg continuation entries.  When guardianDisplayCode
// indicates CONTINUATION (3/4) or TREND EXPANSION (5/6), the Action row
// shows CONT BUY/SELL READY in aqua instead of standard BUY/SELL READY.
// Alert payloads use MB_CONTINUE_LONG/SHORT with type="CONTINUATION".
// Trigger row appends "(Continuation)" context when _isContinuance is true.
// This lets the trader know to HOLD or ADD rather than take a fresh entry.

// v17.69.1 CHANGELOG — ALERT REGISTRATION HOOK
// Add dummy alertcondition(false) so the indicator appears in TradingView's
// "Condition" dropdown when creating alerts.  No logic changes.

// v17.69.0 CHANGELOG — EXECUTION-ONLY ALERT ARCHITECTURE
// PROBLEM: The alert system fires on POI touches, MONITOR transitions, and
//   early-stage setups — creating alert fatigue.  The user receives notifications
//   before a valid trade exists (e.g., WAIT + 66% conf still triggers alerts).
// FIX: Three-tier alert architecture replaces the old two-tier system:
//   Tier 1 (RECON) — INTERNAL ONLY.  HUD updates, state tracking, debug log.
//     NO alert() call.  No webhook.  No mobile notification.
//   Tier 2 (SETUP READY) — OPTIONAL (enableSetupReadyAlerts, default OFF).
//     Fires when: Conf >= 65%, Guardian aligned, HTF/LTF aligned,
//     Sequence >= 4/5, Action == MONITOR.  No webhook execution.
//   Tier 3 (EXECUTE) — PRIMARY.  The only alert that fires by default.
//     Fires ONLY on state transition (WAIT/MONITOR → BUY/SELL READY) when:
//     • Action = BUY READY or SELL READY (or CT variants)
//     • Confidence >= mbAlertConfThresh (raised default to 70)
//     • Guardian aligned with direction
//     • Displacement confirmed (displacementDetected)
//     • MSS confirmed (mssCloseUp/mssCloseDown)
//     • Sequence >= 4 (near-complete or complete)
//     Alert names: MB_EXECUTE_LONG / MB_EXECUTE_SHORT (direction-tagged).
//     Payload upgraded with entry mode, R:R placeholder, and execution fields.
// ANTI-SPAM: var state memory (_prevAction + _prevAlertBar) prevents duplicate
//   alerts while conditions remain unchanged.  Only state TRANSITIONS fire.
// RESULT: ~80-90% reduction in alert volume.  Webhooks = actionable trades only.

// v17.68.1 CHANGELOG — NARRATIVE DIVERGENCE FLAG
// When the H1-anchored Narrative (ebNarrative) differs from the chart-local
// amdState, a ⚠ symbol is appended to the Narrative row.  This prevents
// misreading "ACCUMULATION" on an H4 chart that is locally in MARKDOWN.
// Display-only — H1 anchor logic, ebNarrColor, confidence, triggers, and
// alerts are completely untouched.

// v17.68.0 CHANGELOG — COUNTER-TREND INTELLIGENCE LAYER
// ====
// CONTEXT: The MB (v17.67.9) hard-blocks counter-trend at three points:
//   1) Trigger P3 forces "Need MSS" when sysCounterTrend==true
//   2) Action buyReady/sellReady require isWithTrend (HTF↔LTF agree)
//   3) MB_EXECUTE can never fire since Action never reaches READY during CT
//   This means legitimate reversals (e.g. bullish LTF shift at PDL while
//   HTF is bearish) are invisible.  v17.68.0 adds a controlled CT path.
// D1 — _isCTSetup BOOLEAN: True when ALL three gates pass simultaneously:
//   a) HTF/LTF conflict (sysCounterTrend==true)
//   b) Price at a bias-aligned key level (_proxLevel within _proxTol):
//      • CT long: price near PDL/Daily Low/Asian Low/H4 Demand
//      • CT short: price near PDH/Daily High/Asian High/H4 Supply
//   c) LTF structural confirmation: mssState>=1 in the counter direction
// D2 — TRIGGER P1.5 — CT CATALYST: New priority between P1 and P2.
//   Fires ONLY when _isCTSetup==true AND mbAllowCT input is ON.
//   Output: "CT: Bull Flip at [Level]" / "CT: Bear Flip at [Level]"
//   Color: color.fuchsia.  _trigCtx := 6 (new CT context).
//   If P1 already handled the level (no LTF flip yet), P1 stays in charge.
// D3 — ACTION ROW _trigCtx==6: New CT path in Action row.
//   • _trigCtx==6 + Conf >= mbAlertConfThresh → CT BUY/SELL READY (fuchsia)
//   • _trigCtx==6 + Conf < threshold → CT MONITOR (orange)
// D4 — EXECUTION ALERT: MB_EXECUTE now fires for CT BUY/SELL READY too.
//   Payload includes "type":"COUNTER_TREND" vs "WITH_TREND" field.
// D5 — mbAllowCT INPUT: Boolean toggle (default OFF) in Visual Settings.
//   When OFF, CT path is completely inactive — identical to v17.67.9.
// NOTE: isWithTrend, buyReady, sellReady, and all legacy gates are
//   UNTOUCHED.  CT is an additive parallel lane, not a modification.
//
// ====
// v17.67.9 CHANGELOG — CENTRALIZED MARKET BRIEF ALERT SYSTEM
// ====
// CONTEXT: The legacy alert system (Sniper/Continuation/V-Shape) required
//   perfect alignment across HTF, LTF, Sequence, Momentum, Guardian, and
//   dual-mode gating — resulting in zero alerts over 14+ days of messy but
//   tradable conditions.  The Market Brief already solves this with nuanced
//   states (WAIT/MONITOR/BUY READY/SELL READY) and a Confidence score.
// D1 — DEPRECATE LEGACY ALERTS: All 6 alertcondition() calls and 6 dynamic
//   alert() calls for the old signal types are commented out.  The fire_*
//   booleans, JSON prefix/suffix, consistency checks, and sequence gates
//   remain intact (no runtime removal) so they can be un-commented if
//   needed.  Only the alert emission is silenced.
// D2 — RECON ALERT: Fires once when the MB Action row transitions from
//   any non-MONITOR state to MONITOR.  Uses `var string` to track the
//   previous-bar Action state.  Payload includes symbol, trigger, location,
//   and bias strings for immediate context.
// D3 — EXECUTION ALERT: Fires when Action is BUY READY or SELL READY AND
//   Confidence >= user-adjustable threshold (input, default 50%).  Full
//   MB context in the JSON payload (version, action, confidence, trigger,
//   narrative, location, bias, price, time).
// D4 — DYNAMIC alert() ONLY: Both new alerts use alert() with dynamic
//   string payloads (not alertcondition) so all MB context flows to
//   phone/email/webhook.  freq_once_per_bar_close prevents spam.
// NOTE: The old Market Brief alert (Conf>=66) is replaced by D3.
//   H1 Narrative + M15 LTF remain globally anchored (v17.67.5 fix).
//
// ====
// v17.67.8 CHANGELOG — PROXIMITY & CATALYST OVERHAUL (Trigger Row v5)
// ====
// CONTEXT: v17.67.7 Trigger row prioritised distant structural outcomes
//   (e.g. "Break M5 Supply") over immediate local interactions (e.g. sitting
//   on PDL during bearish Markdown). When price approaches a major HTF
//   support/resistance the card must react to the LOCATION first.
// OVERHAUL: Complete rewrite with Proximity-First hierarchy:
//   P0: Fast-paths (MSS bypass active, alert already live) — unchanged
//   P1: Location Interaction (HIGHEST) — is price within a tight ATR-based
//       tolerance of PDL/PDH/Daily Low/High/Asian H-L/H4 zone?
//       Output: "Watch [Level] Reaction" or "Hold [Level]"
//   P2: Liquidity Sweep & Reclaim — has a level just been swept or is
//       amdState=="MANIPULATION"?  Output: "Sweep & Reclaim" / "Reclaim [Level]"
//   P3: Low-Confidence Structural Shift — Confidence <50% and system
//       rejected/idle → "Need Bullish MSS" / "Need Bearish MSS"
//   P4: Distant Structural Target (lowest) — only when price floats
//       mid-range with established bias → "[Dir] Disp thru [Level]"
// D2 — ATR GUARDRAIL: If the nearest target level is >1.5× ATR away from
//   currentPrice, it is NEVER used as an immediate trigger. Fallback:
//   "Watch Price Action" instead of naming a distant level.
// D3 — ACTION ALIGNMENT via _trigCtx bridge integer:
//   _trigCtx=1 (watching reaction) or 2 (sweep reclaim) → MONITOR (orange)
//   _trigCtx=3 (need MSS) + mssState≥1 → directional READY
//   _trigCtx=4 (distant displacement) → WAIT (yellow)
//   _trigCtx=5 (ready) → BUY/SELL READY as before
// NOTE: H1 Narrative + M15 LTF remain globally anchored (v17.67.5 fix).
//   Only the Trigger row uses hyper-local ATR proximity tracking.
//
// ====
// v17.67.7 CHANGELOG — TACTICAL CATALYST ENGINE (Trigger Row v4)
// ====
// CONTEXT: v17.67.6 Trigger row still showed "Break H4 Supply" when Bullish, which
//   is a destination/target, not an entry trigger. Screenshots showed the H4 chart
//   saying "Break H4 Supply" 100+ pips away — useless for entry timing.
// OVERHAUL: Complete rewrite of Trigger row with "Next Blocker" priority logic:
//   P0: Fast-paths (MSS bypass, alert live) — unchanged
//   P1: Displacement Filter — if system says No Displacement, name the specific
//       local M5/M15 level that needs breaking with displacement language
//   P2: HTF Boundary Warning — if price is INSIDE an H4 zone, warn about
//       rejection/breakout risk (only when touching, never when distant)
//   P3: Local Structure Reclaim — if Bullish but AMD is MARKDOWN/MANIPULATION,
//       trigger is "Reclaim [local supply]" or "Bullish MSS", not upside target
//   P4: Liquidity Sweep — near PDH/PDL/Asian H/L within 5% of range
//   P5: Fallthrough — Seq/KZ/BUY-SELL states
// D2: H4/Daily labels ONLY appear if price is touching them. If nearest obstacle
//   is H4 and distant, defaults to "Wait Local CHoCH" instead.
// D3: Narrative (H1) and LTF (M15) remain global constants as previously fixed.
//
// ====
// v17.67.6 CHANGELOG — MARKET BRIEF INTELLIGENCE & CONSISTENCY UPGRADE
// ====
// DELIVERABLE 1 (H1 Global Narrative): Carried from v17.67.5. Narrative row
//   reads H1 AMD state via request.security, chart-independent.
// DELIVERABLE 2 (M15 Global LTF): Carried from v17.67.4. ltfForceBull/Bear
//   and ltfOverrideActive use M15 ATR + close via request.security.
// DELIVERABLE 3 (Smart Trigger Hierarchy): Replaced "nearest obstacle" logic
//   with a prioritized "What Next" engine:
//     Priority 1: Liquidity Sweep — price within 5% of PDH/PDL/Asian H/L
//     Priority 2: Structural Reversal — bias conflict or OVR → Bullish/Bearish MSS
//     Priority 3: Path Clearance — nearest M5/M15 obstacle (entry gate), NOT H4
//   Falls through to existing Await MSS / Seq / Kill Zone / BUY-SELL states.
// DELIVERABLE 4 (Target vs Trigger): Zones in the "profit direction" (e.g. H4
//   Supply while Bullish) are now labeled "TP: [Zone]" instead of triggers.
//   The Trigger row stays focused on the entry gate.
//
// ====
// v17.67.5 CHANGELOG — NARRATIVE ROW FIXED TO H1 TIMEFRAME
// ====
// CONTEXT: The Narrative row displayed the chart-local AMD state, meaning it
//   showed MARKDOWN on M5 but MARKUP on H4 for the same bar. This made the
//   Market Brief unreliable as a "universal verdict card" when switching TFs.
// FIX: Added request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "60", amdState) to lock the
//   Narrative row to the H1 AMD phase. Falls back to chart-local amdState if
//   H1 data is unavailable. The ebNarrColor now derives from ebNarrative
//   (the fixed value) instead of the raw amdState.
// WHY H1: Fast enough for intraday shifts, slow enough to filter M5 noise,
//   consistent with the strategy's primary analysis timeframe. H4 updates too
//   slowly and would lag real reversals.
//
// ====
// v17.67.4 CHANGELOG — EXECUTIVE MARKET BRIEF V2 UPGRADE
// ====
// CONTEXT: The v17.67.3 Market Brief card needed more precision and specificity
//   in its display rows to reduce ambiguity during rapid pair scanning.
// FIXES:
//   1. BIAS row: Replaced "CONFLICTING" with directional HTF/LTF bias showing
//      which TF dominates (e.g. "HTF Bullish", "LTF Bearish (OVR)"). HTF always
//      carries more weight; LTF OVR flag shown when momentum override is active.
//   2. TRIGGER row: Replaced generic "Await Displacement" with specific structural
//      levels ("Break M5 Supply", "Reject H1 Supply", "Sweep PDH"). Scans MTF
//      zone arrays (M5 → M15 → H1 → H4) to find the nearest actionable level.
//   3. LOCATION row: Added timeframe labels to zone identification. Now shows
//      "H1 Demand (Active)" instead of generic "In Demand Zone". Scans all TF
//      zone arrays to identify which specific zone price occupies.
//   4. ACTION row: Replaced binary AVOID/WAIT with 4-level hierarchy:
//      WAIT (yellow) → MONITOR (orange) → BUY READY (green) → SELL READY (red).
//      Removed AVOID entirely from vocabulary.
//   5. NEW Confidence row: Weighted percentage score (POI 20%, Confluence 25%,
//      Momentum 20%, HTF/LTF Agreement 20%, Location Quality 15%). Color-coded
//      red (0-33%), yellow (34-65%), lime (66-85%), bright green (86-100%). Placed above Action row.
// PRESERVED: Main diagnostic HUD, signal engine, Guardian, P&D anchor, S&D zones,
//   alert engine — all byte-identical to v17.67.3.
// ====
//
// ====
// v17.67.3 CHANGELOG — EXECUTIVE MARKET BRIEF (SCAN & GO VERDICT CARD)
// ====
// CONTEXT: Pair scanning requires reading the full 16-row diagnostic HUD, which
//   takes too long when cycling through watchlist pairs. Traders need a "glance
//   and go" verdict visible in under 3 seconds.
// FIX: Added a compact 5-row "Executive Market Brief" card anchored to the
//   middle-right of the chart (non-overlapping with the main HUD). It synthesizes
//   multi-timeframe data into five rows:
//     Row 1  NARRATIVE — AMD phase (Accumulation / Manipulation / Distribution /
//                        Markup / Markdown) sourced from the existing amdState.
//     Row 2  LOCATION  — Nearest HTF structural point of interest (H4/H1 Supply,
//                        Demand, Premium/Discount, PDH/PDL proximity).
//     Row 3  BIAS      — HTF↔LTF synergy verdict (Bullish / Bearish / Conflicting
//                        / Neutral).
//     Row 4  TRIGGER   — The specific M5/M15 price event needed to confirm bias
//                        (Break Supply, Sweep PDH, MSS Down, Await Displacement…).
//     Row 5  ACTION    — Ultimate verdict with color-coded background:
//                        GREEN  = TRADE READY (all filters passed + momentum > 0)
//                        YELLOW = WAIT / MONITOR (ranging / partial blockers)
//                        RED    = AVOID (counter-trend / heavy rejections)
//   When an MSS-Retrace bypass fires, ACTION immediately switches to
//   "BYPASS TRIGGER" highlighted in green.
// PRESERVED: Main diagnostic HUD (left side) is untouched. Signal engine,
//   Guardian, P&D anchor, S&D zones, alert engine — all byte-identical.
// ====
//
// ====
// v17.67.2 CHANGELOG — MSS-RETRACE BYPASS PATCH (LTF-GATE PRIORITY OVERRIDE)
// ====
// CONTEXT: Trading the 8 AM EST Overlap Breakout (Sweep-Reversal / MSS-Retrace)
// category. The execution gate requires HTF↔LTF alignment (isWithTrend) before an
// EXECUTION-grade signal fires. For MSS-Retrace entries this is too slow: waiting
// for M15 (LTF) structure to flip in the HTF direction means the system misses
// ~80% of the displacement leg that the MSS close already confirmed.
//
// FIX — PRIORITY BYPASS OF THE LTF GATE, SCOPED STRICTLY TO MSS-RETRACE:
//   New booleans (defined right after the AMD phase block, ~after amdPhaseStr):
//     isMssBypassShort = entryModeInput=="MSS-Retrace" AND finalHTFTrend==-1
//                        AND amdState=="MARKDOWN" AND mssCloseDown
//     isMssBypassLong  = entryModeInput=="MSS-Retrace" AND finalHTFTrend== 1
//                        AND amdState=="MARKUP"   AND mssCloseUp
//     isMssBypass      = isMssBypassLong or isMssBypassShort
//   where mssCloseDown = (mssState>=1 and mssDir==-1) or m5BearMSS  (MSS close to
//   the downside), and mssCloseUp = (mssState>=1 and mssDir==1) or m5BullMSS.
//   "Bypass only if HTF bias established" is guaranteed by the finalHTFTrend==±1
//   tests (a NEUTRAL HTF can never satisfy either branch).
//
// WHAT THE BYPASS CHANGES (only when isMssBypass == true):
//   1. isExecutionAllowed — the LTF/Guardian sub-clause "(isWithTrend and
//      isGuardianActive)" gains "... or isMssBypass". This is ADDITIVE: it can
//      only ever PERMIT an execution that the LTF flip-wait would have delayed.
//      The session (isNYSession), POI>=5, blockSignal and alertDirection guards
//      are all UNCHANGED, so a bypass can never fire without a real directional
//      MSS-Retrace signal having already set alertDirection.
//   2. Guardian row — shows "SELL | ACTIVE" (bull: "BUY | ACTIVE") instead of the
//      counter-trend "… | STANDBY".
//   3. Align row — shows "ALIGNED (MSS)" (green) instead of "COUNTER TREND ⚠️".
//   4. System row — shows "Approved: MSS Alignment" instead of a "Rejected: …"
//      blocker headline.
//   (System Status naturally resolves to EXECUTION READY via change #1.)
//
// SAFETY / WHAT IS PRESERVED:
//   • The LTF gate is fully intact for EVERY other path. For any entry that is not
//     entryModeInput=="MSS-Retrace" (Trend Continuation / BOS / V-Shape / etc.)
//     isMssBypass is false, so isExecutionAllowed, Guardian, Align and the System
//     row are byte-for-byte identical to v17.67.1.
//   • No change to P&D anchor, S&D zones, sequence, Gate, momentum or any
//     signal-detection logic. Only the execution-gate OR-term and three HUD
//     display strings are touched, all keyed off the single isMssBypass boolean.
//
// WEBHOOK PAYLOAD (additive — for the SMC Performance Tracker):
//   • Two OPTIONAL fields appended to the alert() JSON suffix:
//       "entry_mode":"<BOS|MSS-Retrace>"   — the active entry mode
//       "mss_bypass":<0|1>                  — 1 when this alert fired via the
//                                             MSS-Retrace bypass, else 0
//     All pre-existing fields, names and ordering are unchanged; existing tracker
//     consumers ignore unknown fields, so this is fully backward-compatible.
// ====
//
// ====
// v17.67.1 CHANGELOG — HUD CLEANUP + "WHY NO ALERT" DIAGNOSTIC + INPUT DEFAULTS
// ====
// DISPLAY / INPUT-DEFAULT ONLY. No signal, alert-engine, Guardian, P&D anchor,
// S&D zone, sequence or trade-entry logic was changed in this version.
//
// 1. MSS ROW REMOVED — the dedicated HUD "MSS" row (WAITING/ACTIVE state) was
//    removed entirely. The underlying mssState/mssDir machine is untouched and
//    still drives the signal engine; only its HUD row was deleted.
//
// 2. HUD ROWS REORDERED to:
//      HTF · LTF · Align · KZ · Sniper · POI · POI+ · Confl · Confl+ · AMD ·
//      Momentum · Guardian · System · Entry · Today · News
//    (AMD moved up above Momentum; System moved down below Guardian.) Optional
//    debug rows were shifted up by one (now rows 17-23) to close the gap.
//
// 3. SYSTEM ROW = "WHY NO ALERT" DIAGNOSTIC. When no execution alert is firing,
//    the System row now explains why, evaluating blockers in priority order:
//      1 Counter Trend → 2 Still in Discount/Premium → 3 LTF Bullish/Bearish →
//      4 No Displacement → 5 Sequence Incomplete (X/5, uses confluencePillarScore
//      from the Confl row) → 6 Awaiting MSS → 7 Outside Kill Zone →
//      8 Guardian Standby → 9 ACTIVE ALERT: [dir] → 10 SCANNING.
//    Up to the 2 most-important blockers are combined with " | "; the second is
//    placed on its own line so the cell wraps vertically without widening the
//    table. The existing trade counter T:active/maxDaily is preserved on line 2.
//    This block is strictly read-only (reads finalized state, writes nothing back).
//
// 4. BOS SWING LENGTH default changed 5 → 10 (input.int "BOS Swing Length").
//
// 5. PDH/PDL LINE COLOR defaults changed to color.new(#00BCD4, 0) (cyan/teal).
// ====
//
// ====
// v17.67.0 CHANGELOG — P&D ORIGIN: DISPLACEMENT-ORIGIN ANCHOR SELECTION
// ====
// PROBLEM (v17.66.9): On a structural flip the origin was anchored to the most
// recent PHASE EXTREME (prevPhaseLowestLow / prevPhaseHighestHigh). On most pairs
// the phase extreme happens to coincide with the displacement-origin swing, so 6
// pairs (AUDUSD, NZDUSD, USDCHF, GBPUSD, EURGBP, USDCAD) anchored correctly. But
// on EURUSD and GBPJPY the most-recent phase extreme was an INTERNAL swing — a
// minor pullback low inside a bullish expansion (GBPJPY) or an internal swing
// high inside a bearish leg (EURUSD) — NOT the swing that actually launched the
// displacement. Result: the P&D zone anchored to an internal pivot, mis-placing
// premium/discount levels on those two pairs.
//
// FIX — ANCHOR TO THE DISPLACEMENT-ORIGIN SWING (the BOS-triggering pivot):
//   A BOS is, by definition, price breaking the last confirmed swing pivot. The
//   swing that LAUNCHED that displacement is the OPPOSITE pivot that immediately
//   preceded the break:
//     • Bullish BOS  = close breaks ABOVE bos_lastPH  ⇒ the launching swing LOW
//       is bos_lastPL (the last confirmed pivot low before the break).
//     • Bearish BOS  = close breaks BELOW bos_lastPL  ⇒ the launching swing HIGH
//       is bos_lastPH (the last confirmed pivot high before the break).
//   So the flip blocks now anchor:
//     • isBullishFlip : activeOriginLow  := bos_lastPL   (was prevPhaseLowestLow)
//     • isBearishFlip : activeOriginHigh := bos_lastPH   (was prevPhaseHighestHigh)
//   These are the actual displacement-origin swings, not general phase extremes.
//
// WHAT IS PRESERVED:
//   • Within-leg "extend outward only" (math.min / math.max) maintenance — origin
//     still cannot ratchet toward price on continuation bars, and can still deepen
//     to a truer macro extreme if structure extends.
//   • v17.66.8 flip-bar contamination guard and v17.66.9 CHoCH-sensitive reset.
//   • All signals, Gate, Guardian, sequence, alerts, S&D zones, HUD, webhook —
//     UNCHANGED. Only the origin anchor SOURCE in the two flip blocks changed.
//   • bos_lastPH / bos_lastPL already exist (defined at the BOS pivot-memory block
//     via request.security pivots, lookahead_off) — no new tracking was needed.
//
// EXPECTED RESULT: EURUSD anchors to the higher swing high that launched the
//   bearish displacement; GBPJPY anchors to the lowest swing low that launched
//   the bullish expansion. The other 6 pairs are unaffected because their phase
//   extreme already equalled the displacement-origin pivot.
// ====
//
// ====
// v17.66.9 CHANGELOG — MACRO TREND: CHoCH-SENSITIVE RESET (Option 2)
// ====
// PROBLEM (v17.66.8): The macroTrend flip required price to CLOSE BELOW the
// locked activeOriginLow (bull) or ABOVE activeOriginHigh (bear) before a
// re-anchor was allowed. On pairs like EURUSD/AUDUSD with a deep historical
// origin (e.g. 0.55086), this condition was never met, so the P&D zone was
// permanently anchored to a fossil low/high — even with Zone Source = RECENT.
//
// FIX — CHoCH-TRIGGERED RE-ANCHOR:
//   The "origin must be broken" guard is removed from the macroTrend transition.
//   Any confirmed BOS in the OPPOSITE direction of the current leg is now treated
//   as a Change of Character (CHoCH) and triggers an immediate flip + re-anchor.
//   This matches the video methodology (The Trading Geek): when structure shifts,
//   re-draw the Fib tool to the NEW swing — do not wait for the old origin to be
//   re-tested.
//
//   bullOriginBroken / bearOriginBroken are retained as `false` booleans to
//   preserve downstream compatibility with rangeForceExpanded (no other code
//   changes required).
//
// WHAT IS PRESERVED:
//   • Within-leg "extend outward only" (math.min / math.max) — origin still
//     cannot ratchet toward price on continuation bars.
//   • v17.66.8 phase-tracker snapshot ordering fix — flip bar contamination
//     prevention is fully intact.
//   • All signals, Gate, Guardian, HUD, alerts, MTF S&D engine — UNCHANGED.
//
// EXPECTED RESULT: originLow / originHigh will now reflect the most recent
//   structural swing, consistent with Zone Source = RECENT intent.
// ====
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.8 CHANGELOG — P&D ORIGIN: PHASE-TRACKER ORDERING FIX (no deletion)
// ============================================================================
// PROBLEM: the running phase-extreme trackers (phaseLowestLow / phaseHighestHigh)
// were updated at the TOP of the bar, BEFORE the flip/BOS anchor logic ran, so a
// flip could read a tracker already mutated by the current (flip) bar — letting
// the flip bar's own forming extreme contaminate the new origin anchor instead of
// using the COMPLETED prior-phase structure.
//
// REJECTED FIX: simply deleting the two top-of-loop tracker updates. That would
// stop the trackers from following the running prior-phase low/high during a
// move, re-introducing the v17.66.6 "stranded origin" bug (the flip would anchor
// to a stale reset value, not the true prior-phase extreme). Verified by sim.
//
// APPLIED FIX (sequencing, not deletion):
//   1. PRE-FLIP SNAPSHOT: prevPhaseLowestLow / prevPhaseHighestHigh capture the
//      tracker value BEFORE this bar's running update. The running min/max update
//      is PRESERVED immediately after the snapshot.
//   2. The flip blocks now read the SNAPSHOT (prevPhase*) instead of the live
//      tracker, so the anchor is always the completed prior-phase extreme on
//      closed bars and can never include the current flip bar.
//   3. The within-leg "extend outward only" maintenance is SKIPPED on the flip bar
//      (`and not isBullishFlip` / `and not isBearishFlip`) so the flip bar's own
//      extreme cannot override the freshly-set prior-phase anchor on the same bar.
//      On every subsequent continuation bar it runs unchanged (still deepens to a
//      truer macro low/high — the v17.66.6 behaviour is preserved).
//
// VALIDATION (logic simulation, all PASS):
//   • Decline to true low 0.7815 → bullish flip ⇒ activeOriginLow = 0.7815.
//   • Rally to true high 0.7990 → bearish flip ⇒ activeOriginHigh = 0.7990.
//   • Flip bar that WICKS to a new extreme (0.8050) ⇒ anchor stays 0.7990 (the
//     completed prior-phase high), NOT the flip bar's wick.
//   • Deeper true low printed on a continuation bar still deepens the origin.
//   • Minor pullback inside a leg still cannot ratchet the origin toward price.
// Nothing else changed (inputs, labels, HUD, alerts, visuals, signals untouched).
// ============================================================================
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.6 CHANGELOG — P&D ORIGIN: "STRANDED HIGH ORIGIN" ROOT-CAUSE FIX
// ============================================================================
// SYMPTOM (user screenshot, USDCHF H4): in a bull leg whose TRUE macro low was
// ~0.7815, the DISCOUNT origin sat stranded at ~0.7930 (a higher, earlier pivot)
// and never dropped to the real swing low.
//
// ROOT CAUSE (what v17.66.3/4/5 all missed):
//   v17.66.5 made the origin a HARD LOCK that is re-anchored ONLY on a structural
//   flip. That correctly stopped the origin from ratcheting UP onto minor
//   pullbacks — BUT it also made the origin unable to DEEPEN to the true macro
//   low when that low is printed AFTER a weak early establishment and WITHOUT a
//   confirmed bearish flip. Sequence that strands it:
//     1. Early weak bull establishment anchors activeOriginLow at 0.7930.
//     2. Price later prints a deeper TRUE low 0.7815 with NO bearish BOS/flip.
//     3. macroTrend stays bullish (correct), but the locked origin is frozen at
//        0.7930, so the discount bottom is stranded ABOVE the real low. ← BUG
//
// THE FIX — ORIGIN EXTENDS OUTWARD ONLY (never inward / never up):
//   Within an established leg the origin is no longer frozen; it tracks the
//   running structural extreme but can move in ONE direction only:
//     • Bull leg : activeOriginLow  := math.min(activeOriginLow,  low)
//                  → can only move DOWN to the true swing low; math.min makes it
//                    mathematically IMPOSSIBLE to ratchet UP onto a pullback.
//     • Bear leg : activeOriginHigh := math.max(activeOriginHigh, high)
//                  → can only move UP to the true swing high; never down.
//   It is still re-anchored authoritatively on a genuine flip (to the prior
//   phase's macro extreme). A minor pullback to 0.7930 inside a 0.7815-origin
//   leg leaves the origin at 0.7815 (math.min(0.7815,0.7930)=0.7815). A deeper
//   real low 0.7700 would correctly DEEPEN the origin to 0.7700.
//   Termination continues to extend the opposite side (max high / min low).
//
// WHY THIS IS THE CORRECT SMC BEHAVIOUR:
//   The dealing-range origin is the lowest point of the impulse that remains
//   un-violated by a bearish CHoCH. Until a real flip, the lowest low IS the
//   origin. Extending outward captures it; it can never be pulled toward price.
//
// Everything else (robust macroTrend flip detection, legacy bosTrend semantics,
// Gate/Guardian/sequence/momentum/HUD/webhook/MTF S&D engine) is unchanged.
// ============================================================================
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.5 CHANGELOG — P&D ORIGIN HARD-LOCK: ROOT-CAUSE FIX (2 bugs)
// ============================================================================
//  RANGE-anchoring fix. Signal-firing conditions, the Gate, Guardian, alerts and
//  the MTF S&D engine are unchanged. Only WHERE the H4 P&D origin anchor sits.
//
//  This is the DEFINITIVE fix after v17.66.3 / v17.66.4 still let the DISCOUNT
//  (bull) / PREMIUM (bear) origin ratchet onto minor internal pullbacks. Two
//  independent bugs were found by auditing EVERY write to the origin vars:
//
//  BUG #1 — THE "STRANDED PRICE" SAFETY CLAMP RE-WROTE THE ORIGIN EVERY BAR.
//    The v17.59 expansion/clamp block contained, on ordinary (non-BOS) bars:
//        if bosTrend == 1 ... activeOriginLow := bosRangeLow   // and bear mirror
//    so the supposedly "locked" origin was reassigned continuously. This was the
//    hidden leak the previous 3 versions never removed.
//
//  BUG #2 — MINOR COUNTER-TREND BOS CAUSED SPURIOUS "FLIPS".
//    trendState flipped on ANY bearish BOS (bosSwingLength = 5 H4 bars), even a
//    shallow pullback inside a strong bull leg. The next bullish BOS then looked
//    like a brand-new leg and RESET activeOriginLow to a recent minor pivot low
//    — exactly the upward ratchet seen on the chart.
//
//  FIX:
//    1. NEW robust `macroTrend` that flips ONLY on a GENUINE structural reversal:
//       a bullish leg persists until price CLOSES BELOW the locked bullish origin
//       (bearish leg until close ABOVE the locked bearish origin). Minor counter-
//       trend BOS that do NOT break the locked origin are IGNORED.
//    2. Origin variables (activeOriginLow / activeOriginHigh) are now written in
//       EXACTLY ONE place each — inside `if isBullishFlip` / `if isBearishFlip`.
//       ALL origin writes were removed from the expansion/clamp block; that block
//       was rewritten to extend ONLY the termination side.
//    3. On a flip the origin anchors to the TRUE macro swing extreme of the move
//       (running lowest-low / highest-high), not the most recent minor pivot.
//    4. CONTINUATION never touches the origin — it only extends the termination.
//    5. Optional debug table (input "Show P&D BOS Debug", default OFF) shows
//       bosTrend, macroTrend, flip/continuation and the live origin values.
//  Legacy bosTrend keeps its original per-BOS semantics so every downstream
//  consumer (sequence reset, momentum, HUD, webhook) is byte-for-byte unchanged.
//  All pivots remain CLOSED-bar (request.security, lookahead_off).
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.4 CHANGELOG — P&D BOS: EXPLICIT TREND-STATE FLIP vs CONTINUATION
// ============================================================================
//  RANGE-anchoring refinement. Signal-firing conditions, the Gate, Guardian,
//  alerts and the MTF S&D engine are unchanged. Only WHERE the H4 P&D origin
//  anchor sits is affected.
//
//  PROBLEM (v17.66.3): The flip-vs-continuation decision was derived implicitly
//  from bosTrend, and the CONTINUATION branch still RE-ASSIGNED the origin every
//  BOS via `activeOriginLow := math.min(activeOriginLow, bos_lastPL)` (and the
//  bearish math.max mirror). Although math.min/max usually held the value, the
//  origin was still being touched on every continuation BOS, which is fragile
//  and made the "lock" hard to audit.
//
//  FIX — EXPLICIT TREND STATE + HARD LOCK:
//    • NEW persistent `var int trendState` (1 = bullish, -1 = bearish, 0 = init)
//      is the single source of truth for the active structural leg.
//    • TREND FLIP  (trendState moves FROM {-1,0} TO 1, or FROM {1,0} TO -1):
//        – a brand-new structural leg begins → RESET the origin anchor
//          (activeOriginLow = initiating swing low for bull, activeOriginHigh =
//          initiating swing high for bear) and seed the termination.
//    • CONTINUATION BOS (trendState already equals the BOS direction):
//        – origin anchor is LEFT COMPLETELY UNTOUCHED (no re-assignment at all);
//          ONLY activeTerminationHigh (bull) / activeTerminationLow (bear)
//          extends toward the new structural extreme.
//    • bosTrend is kept in lock-step with trendState so every downstream
//      consumer (sequence reset, momentum, HUD, webhook) is unchanged.
//  Pivots remain CLOSED-bar only (request.security, lookahead_off). The 50/50
//  Premium/Discount split, equilibrium midpoint and all visuals are unchanged.
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.3 CHANGELOG — P&D STRUCTURAL BOS ANCHORING: LOCK MACRO SWING ORIGIN
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY/RANGE change. Signal-firing conditions, the Gate, Guardian, alerts
//  and the MTF S&D engine are unchanged. This ONLY changes WHERE the H4
//  Premium/Discount (P&D) range anchors sit.
//
//  PROBLEM (v17.66.2 and earlier): The BOS-anchored range (v17.58) re-anchored
//  the range bottom/top to the MOST RECENT minor pivot on EVERY confirmed BOS,
//  including continuation BOS inside the same leg:
//      if bosBull: bosRangeLow := bos_lastPL   // <- latest minor pivot low
//  On a large bullish leg 0.7800 → 0.8000, a minor pullback to 0.7930 forms a
//  new pivot low; the next continuation BOS then ratcheted the Discount/origin
//  anchor UP to 0.7930, abandoning the true structural origin (0.7800). The
//  zone "forgot" the macro swing and chased minor internal retracements.
//
//  FIX — STRUCTURAL MACRO ANCHORS (locked until trend FLIP):
//    • activeOriginLow       = lowest confirmed H4 swing low that INITIATED the
//                              current bullish leg (LOCKED at the leg's first BOS)
//    • activeTerminationHigh = highest confirmed H4 swing high of the bullish leg
//    • activeOriginHigh      = highest confirmed H4 swing high that INITIATED the
//                              current bearish leg (LOCKED at the leg's first BOS)
//    • activeTerminationLow  = lowest confirmed H4 swing low of the bearish leg
//  The ORIGIN is set ONLY when the trend flips (a brand-new structural leg). On
//  continuation BOS within the same leg the origin stays put — only the
//  termination extends toward the new structural extreme. Anchors therefore move
//  ONLY on a genuine structural event, never on minor internal pullbacks. All
//  pivots are taken from CLOSED H4 candles (request.security, lookahead_off) so
//  there is no repaint. The 50/50 Premium/Discount split, equilibrium midpoint
//  and all visuals/labels (PREMIUM/DISCOUNT/EQUILIBRIUM) are unchanged.
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.2 CHANGELOG — MTF S&D ZONE INVALIDATION: HARDENED + DOCUMENTED
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY-ONLY change. Signal engine, the Gate, bias, Guardian, POI scoring and
//  every alert()/alertcondition() are byte-for-byte identical to v17.66.1.
//
//  GOAL: Guarantee MTF Supply/Demand zones (H4, H1, M15) are removed from the
//  chart the moment price CLOSES through them, eliminating stale-zone clutter.
//
//  WHAT CHANGED in f_maintainMtfZones():
//    • Added an explicit empty-array guard (if array.size(_arr) > 0) so the
//      maintenance pass is a no-op on timeframes with no active zones.
//    • Split the break test into clearly-named _supplyBroken / _demandBroken
//      booleans so the supply (close > top) and demand (close < bot) cases are
//      individually auditable.
//    • Mark the zone inactive (_z.active := false) before deleting so any later
//      reference cannot treat a deleted box as live.
//    • box.delete(_z.zbox) removes the box AND its embedded text label in one
//      call (MTF labels are drawn via box.new(... text=...), not as separate
//      label objects — so there is no orphaned label to clean up).
//    • array.remove() during back-to-front iteration keeps indices valid.
//  Behavior is functionally identical to v17.66.1 (which already invalidated on
//  close-through); this revision makes the rule explicit, robust and commented.

// ============================================================================
// v17.66.1 CHANGELOG — V-SHAPE UNFILTERED: BYPASS GUARDIAN + COUNTER-TREND + HTF
// ============================================================================
//  V-SHAPE-ONLY change. Every other circuit (MSS-Retrace / Sniper / Tier-2 /
//  Building / Lite / CT-Lite / Re-Entry, the state-machine, Guardian, the
//  counter-trend 5-point filter, POI/confluence scoring, S&D rendering, HUD and
//  all non-V-SHAPE alerts) is untouched. Guardian and the CT filter still gate
//  every OTHER signal exactly as before — only V-SHAPE now ignores them.
//
//  V-SHAPE is now the MOST AGGRESSIVE, unfiltered breakout entry. Removed filters:
//    • vShapeLongRaw / vShapeShortRaw  : DROPPED biasAlignedLong / biasAlignedShort
//        (no HTF trend alignment required — counter-trend setups allowed).
//    • vShapeLongF   / vShapeShortF    : DROPPED ctFilterPassLong / ctFilterPassShort
//        (counter-trend 5-point hard gate no longer applied — pass-through).
//    • vShapeLongFire/ vShapeShortFire : DROPPED (guardian*Actionable or not
//        enableGuardian) — Guardian is bypassed completely.
//
//  V-SHAPE now fires on ONLY three core conditions: (A) valid S&D zone exists,
//  (B) liquidity swept, (C) strong displacement breakout candle. Non-trend
//  structural gates are retained (confirmed bar, state-machine IDLE, Kill Zone,
//  cooldown, new-zone de-dup) since they are not Guardian/CT/HTF filters.
// ============================================================================
// v17.66.0 CHANGELOG — 05:30 SESSION OPEN + V-SHAPE IMMEDIATE BREAKOUT ENTRY
// ============================================================================
//  ADDITIVE update. Every v17.65.6 circuit is preserved byte-for-byte: the
//  MSS-Retrace / Sniper / Tier-2 / Building / Lite / CT-Lite / Re-Entry signal
//  engine, the state-machine ("The Gate"), Guardian HTF-gate, the counter-trend
//  5-point hard filter, POI/confluence scoring, S&D zone rendering, MTF
//  propagation, the HUD and all existing alert()/alertcondition() calls are
//  unchanged. This version only (a) re-times the session open and (b) ADDS a
//  brand-new parallel entry mode.
//
//  1. SESSION OPEN MOVED 08:00 → 05:30 EST  (capture early opening overlap)
//       • New minute-precision helpers estMinute / estMinOfDay and the input
//         pair nyAMStart(=5) + nyAMStartMin(=30) define the 05:30 EST open.
//       • isNYSession now starts at 05:30 (was 08:00); isLondonSession ends at
//         05:30 so the combined isTradeSession window (03:00–12:00) is intact.
//       • isNYAM() Kill Zone now opens 05:30 (was 08:00). seqExecNow = isNYSession
//         therefore also honours the earlier open — every session-based filter
//         and timing check inherits the change automatically.
//
//  2. V-SHAPE IMMEDIATE BREAKOUT ENTRY  (NEW, parallel to MSS-Retrace)
//       Detects liquidity-grab-and-go "V" moves: price sweeps a prior swing
//       (liquidity capture) and leaves a valid S&D zone on a strong displacement
//       candle (body ≥ 70% of range AND ≥ 1.0× ATR). Enters IMMEDIATELY on the
//       breakout close — no retest required — while still passing EVERY existing
//       gate (Guardian, CT 5-point filter, Kill Zone, H4 invalidation, state
//       machine, cooldown). Inputs: enableVShape / vShapeBodyRatio / vShapeDispMin.
//       Feeds anyLongFired/anyShortFired (so SL/TP & state machine reuse the
//       standard zone-based stop placement) and fires its own V-SHAPE alerts.
// ============================================================================
// v17.65.6 CHANGELOG — MTF BOX ANCHOR: STATE TRACKING (replaces fixed offset)
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY-ONLY change. Signal engine, the Gate, bias, Guardian, POI/confluence
//  scoring and every alert()/alertcondition() are byte-for-byte identical to
//  v17.65.5.
//
//  PROBLEM (reported via 5M NZDUSD screenshot, Asian session):
//    The "M15 DEMAND" box floated mid-chart, its left edge disconnected from the
//    candle that formed it. v17.65.5 anchored the left edge at
//        bar_index − round(MTF_minutes / chart_minutes)
//    i.e. a FIXED CHART-BAR COUNT (M15→3, H1→12, H4→48 on a 5M chart). That only
//    maps to the real formation candle when EVERY chart slot has a bar. During
//    thin/illiquid forex windows (Asian session, holidays, low-liquidity) 5M bars
//    are SPARSE, so "N bars back" ≠ "N×chart_min minutes back" and the left edge
//    drifts — the box appears to float away from its origin candle.
//
//  FIX — record the REAL formation bar (state tracking):
//    Two persistent state vars per TF track the bar_index where each HTF candle
//    OPENS:
//        {tf}CurStart  = open-bar of the currently-forming HTF candle
//        {tf}PrevStart = open-bar of the previous (just-closed) HTF candle
//    On each new-HTF-bar event (ta.change(time(tf))) we shift Cur→Prev and set
//    Cur=bar_index. Because zones are detected from the just-CLOSED candle's OHLC
//    (request.security open[1]/high[1]/low[1]/close[1]), {tf}PrevStart is exactly
//    that candle's open bar. The box LEFT edge is pinned to it — gap-proof, no
//    fixed-bar-count assumption. Right edge stays bar_index+10 (only edge that
//    maintenance extends); left edge is clamped to [0, bar_index] and creation is
//    skipped until a valid PrevStart exists (na on the very first HTF bar).
//
//  All v17.65.5 features preserved: M15-prefix TF labels ("M15 SUPPLY/DEMAND"),
//  HUD POI+/Confl+ "-" inactive format, BLACK S&D + P&D zone labels, orange
//  supply / green demand palette, top-down MTF propagation, dynamic right-edge
//  extension, and close-through invalidation.
// ============================================================================
// v17.65.5 CHANGELOG — MTF BOX LEFT-EDGE ANCHOR FIX + M15 LABEL + HUD "-" FORMAT
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY-ONLY change. Signal engine, the Gate, bias, Guardian, POI/confluence
//  scoring and every alert()/alertcondition() are byte-for-byte identical to
//  v17.65.4.
//
//  1. MTF ZONE LEFT-EDGE ANCHOR FIX (primary)
//       H4/H1/M15 Supply & Demand boxes were anchored at the CURRENT bar_index,
//       making every higher-TF zone appear to originate "now" on the 5M chart.
//       They are now anchored at their historical FORMATION bar:
//         offsetBars = round(MTF_minutes / chart_minutes)
//         (on a 5M chart: H4→48 bars, H1→12 bars, M15→3 bars back)
//       Left edge = bar_index − offsetBars (clamped to chart history); right
//       edge stays bar_index + 10 and is the ONLY edge maintenance extends.
//       The trader can now see WHERE each H4/H1/M15 zone actually formed.
//
//  2. M15 TIMEFRAME LABEL FORMAT
//       Intraday-minute zone tags now use the M-prefix ("M15 SUPPLY" /
//       "M15 DEMAND") to match the H4/H1 convention. Labels remain BLACK text
//       on the orange (supply) / green (demand) palette.
//
//  3. HUD "POI+" / "CONFL+" ROWS → DASH FOR INACTIVE
//       Active items render as the plain abbreviation; inactive items render as
//       a single dash "-" (no brackets). Examples:
//         POI+   :  SH | - | MSS | - | -
//         Confl+ :  ALIGN | KZ | - | SWEEP | -
//       Booleans and scoring (poiScore5 / confluencePillarScore) are unchanged.
//
//  4. All v17.65.4 features preserved: BLACK S&D + P&D zone labels, orange
//     supply / green demand palette, top-down MTF propagation, dynamic
//     right-edge extension, and close-through invalidation.
// ============================================================================
// v17.65.4 CHANGELOG — BLACK ZONE LABELS + NAMED POI+/CONFL+ HUD BREAKDOWNS
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY-ONLY change. Signal engine, the Gate, bias, Guardian, POI scoring and
//  every alert()/alertcondition() are byte-for-byte identical to v17.65.3.
//
//  1. S&D ZONE LABELS → BLACK
//       All Supply/Demand zone text labels (H4, H1, M15, and Current-TF) now
//       render in color.black instead of white, for better legibility against
//       the orange/green zone fills. Timeframe tags ("H4 SUPPLY", "M15 DEMAND",
//       "5M DEMAND", ...) and the orange/green palette are unchanged.
//
//  2. P&D ZONE LABELS → BLACK
//       The Premium and Discount H4 zones now carry black "PREMIUM"/"DISCOUNT"
//       text labels (left-anchored), and the Equilibrium line gains a black
//       "EQUILIBRIUM" label (delete-redraw, no price-scale artifact).
//
//  3. HUD "POI+" ROW → NAMED 5-STAGE POI PATH
//       Replaces the generic ✓/· glyphs with the explicit SMC development path:
//         SH | FVG | MSS | Mit | Flip
//       Active stage(s) are highlighted by bracket-wrapping (e.g. "[SH]").
//         SH=Sweep/liquidity grab · FVG=fair-value gap · MSS=structure shift+OB ·
//         Mit=P/D retrace & mitigation · Flip=S/D failure & structural flip.
//       Booleans are display-only (poiDirSweep/poiDirFvg/ltfShiftDetected/
//       poiDirOb/state4Complete/poiDirEq/priceInFlipZone); poiScore5 untouched.
//
//  4. HUD "CONFL+" ROW → NAMED 5 CONFLUENCE PILLARS
//       Replaces the generic ✓/· glyphs with the explicit pillars:
//         ALIGN | KZ | P&D | SWEEP | DISP
//       Active pillar(s) are highlighted by bracket-wrapping (e.g. "[KZ]").
//         ALIGN=LTF matches H4 bias · KZ=kill-zone timing · P&D=bias-aligned
//         premium/discount price · SWEEP=liquidity sweep · DISP=displacement.
//       Display-only; confluencePillarScore / confluenceScore untouched.
//
//  All v17.65.3 behaviour (top-down MTF propagation, dynamic right-edge
//  extension, close-through invalidation) is fully preserved.
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.65.3 CHANGELOG — TOP-DOWN MTF PROPAGATION + UNIFIED PALETTE + TF LABELS
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY-ONLY change. Signal engine, the Gate, bias, Guardian, POI scoring and
//  every alert()/alertcondition() are byte-for-byte identical to v17.65.2.
//
//  1. TOP-DOWN MTF PROPAGATION
//       H4 / H1 / M15 S&D zones now render on ALL equal-or-lower chart
//       timeframes. They are computed via request.security() and painted onto
//       the current chart, so a 5M chart shows H4 + H1 + M15 + local 5M zones
//       overlaid together for confluence. A new propagation gate
//       (allowH4SD/allowH1SD/allowM15SD, derived from timeframe.in_seconds)
//       suppresses a TF's zones only when the chart is ABOVE that TF (you won't
//       see "M15 zones" on an H4 chart).
//
//  2. STANDARDIZED COLOUR SCHEME (all timeframes incl. Current TF)
//       • Supply → fill color.new(color.orange, 85) (15% opacity) + solid orange
//         border, width 2.
//       • Demand → fill color.new(color.green, 85) (15% opacity) + solid green
//         border, width 2.
//       The old per-TF palette (red/blue, orange/teal, pink/aqua) is removed;
//       timeframe is now identified by the LABEL, not the colour.
//
//  3. WHITE CENTERED TF LABELS ON EVERY ZONE
//       Each active box carries a centered white text label naming its TF + type:
//       "H4 SUPPLY", "H1 DEMAND", "M15 SUPPLY", and the local zones read
//       "5M DEMAND" / "15M SUPPLY" (curTfTag prefix; FLIP marker preserved).
//
//  4. v17.65.2 DYNAMIC LOGIC PRESERVED
//       MtfZone UDT, right-edge extension to bar_index + 10 each bar, and
//       close-through invalidation (supply: close > top; demand: close < bot)
//       are all retained unchanged.
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.65.2 CHANGELOG — MTF S&D ZONES: DYNAMIC EXTEND + CLOSE-THROUGH INVALIDATION
// ============================================================================
//  DISPLAY-ONLY change. Signal engine, the Gate, bias, Guardian, POI scoring and
//  every alert()/alertcondition() are byte-for-byte identical to v17.65.1.
//
//  PROBLEM (v17.65.1): The Multi-Timeframe S&D zones (H4/H1/M15) were drawn as
//  STATIC 20-bar boxes — box.new(bar_index, top, bar_index + 20, bot). They:
//    • never extended toward live price (stuck at a fixed width),
//    • never invalidated when price traded through them, and
//    • accumulated into overlapping clutter that obscured the chart.
//
//  FIX:
//    1. NEW UDT `MtfZone {box zbox; float top; float bot; bool isSupply; bool
//       active}` replaces the old raw `array<box>` per-direction tracking. The
//       6 supply/demand arrays collapse into 3 combined arrays (h4/h1/m15Zones)
//       so geometry + state travel with each box.
//    2. `f_createMtfZone()` (renamed from f_plotMtfZone) now spawns the box with
//       its RIGHT edge at the current bar (was bar_index + 20).
//    3. NEW `f_maintainMtfZones()` runs EVERY bar and, for each active zone:
//         • TF toggle OFF  → box.delete() + array.remove()  (instant clean-up)
//         • CLOSED through  → INVALIDATE: supply if close > top, demand if
//                             close < bot (confirmed bar only) → delete + remove
//         • otherwise       → box.set_right(bar_index)  (extend to live price)
//       Back-to-front iteration makes array.remove() during the loop safe.
//    Result: only active, untested MTF zones remain on the chart, each tracking
//    live price exactly like the primary-TF zones — clean during the 08:00–12:00
//    EST window. Memory still trimmed to MAX_ZONES_PER_TF per timeframe.
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.62.0 CHANGELOG — DIRECTIONAL POI + 5-PILLAR CONFLUENCE + HUD CONSOLIDATION
// ============================================================================
//  ALL CHANGES IN THIS VERSION ARE DISPLAY-ONLY. The signal-generation engine,
//  the state machine ("The Gate"), and every alert()/alertcondition() call are
//  byte-for-byte identical to v17.60.1. NO trade logic was modified.
//
//  - FEATURE 1 — DIRECTIONAL POI SCORE (HUD "POI" row → X/3):
//        New display-only counter `poiDirScore` (max 3). It counts the
//        directional confluence components that AGREE with the active HTF bias:
//          LONG  bias → Bullish FVG + Bullish OB + Discount EQ
//          SHORT bias → Bearish FVG + Bearish OB + Premium EQ
//        This is SEPARATE from the core `poiScore` (signal logic) and the
//        existing `poiScoreDisplay`. Neither is mutated. (v17.56.8 pattern.)
//  - FEATURE 2 — 5-PILLAR CONFLUENCE SCORE (HUD "Confl" row → X/5):
//        New display-only score `confluencePillarScore` (max 5):
//          (1) Location  → directional POI fully aligned (poiDirScore >= 3)
//          (2) Timing    → Kill Zone active
//          (3) Direction → HTF and LTF trend aligned (same non-zero direction)
//          (4) Momentum  → displacement active OR a BOS present
//          (5) Readiness → Sniper Progress (dtStage) >= 4
//        SEPARATE from the core `confluenceScore`/`confluenceRaw` (signal logic
//        + plot 8). Neither is mutated; plot count is unchanged.
//  - FEATURE 3 — HUD CONSOLIDATION (net −2 always-visible rows):
//        * Stage + Alert + Trades merged into ONE "System" row:
//              "{stage} | {alert} | T:{active}/{maxDaily}"
//          (alert segment still shows "NO ACTIVE ALERT" when stale).
//        * New "POI+" breakdown row → "[S | O | F | E]" (Sweep/OB/FVG/EQ),
//          colored green for LONG bias, red for SHORT, grey when inactive.
//        * Standalone SniperTr / ActiveTr rows folded into System.
//        * Optional debug/sequence/override rows shifted up by 2 (21–34 → 19–32).
//        * New display-only input "Max Daily Trades (HUD display)" (default 3).
//  - UI: HUD text reverted to size.small (from v17.61 size.normal) for
//        f_setCell/f_setHdrCell; debug rows remain size.tiny.
//  - PRESERVED from v17.60.1: Align row consistency (finalHTFTrend/finalLTFTrend),
