// v17.60.1 CHANGELOG — HUD CONSISTENCY BUGFIX (display-only)
// ============================================================================
//  - BUG R1 (CRITICAL): The "Align" row showed "WITH TREND" even when the HTF
//        and LTF rows displayed opposite directions (e.g. HTF BEARISH +
//        LTF BULLISH on GBPUSD/EURGBP/EURUSD). Root cause: Align was computed
//        from the RAW structural biases (htfBias/ltfBias) instead of the
//        override-adjusted values actually shown (finalHTFTrend/finalLTFTrend).
//        FIX: Align now compares the SAME finalized variables rendered in the
//        HTF/LTF rows — apples-to-apples. match → "WITH TREND ✅" (green),
//        mismatch → "COUNTER TREND ⚠️" (orange), either neutral → "NEUTRAL".
//        NOTE: the alert-side isWithTrend/isCounterTrend/alertAlign are LEFT
//        UNTOUCHED so alert firing & webhook behaviour are byte-identical.
//  - BUG R2 (MEDIUM): The "Guardian" row direction token could contradict the
//        HTF/LTF/Align rows (e.g. NZDUSD HTF BULL + LTF BULL → "SELL"). The
//        Guardian is an EXECUTION-PERMISSION filter, not a competing bias, so
//        its directional token now follows the displayed HTF trend
//        (finalHTFTrend). The action token (EXECUTE/STANDBY), colour, CONFLICT
//        and counter-trend REVERSAL semantics are preserved.
//  - FEATURE R3: New "Show Alignment Debug" input (group "🔧 Debug", default
//        OFF) adds an auditable HUD row showing the raw HTF / LTF / Match /
//        Guardian values used by the consistency logic. maxHudRows 34 → 35.
//  - Non-functional: NO changes to signal generation, alert firing/messages,
//        the state machine (The Gate), or any calculations. Display layer only.
