// ============================================================================
// v17.59.1 CHANGELOG — UX POLISH: Alert HUD Cleanup
// ============================================================================
// [2026-06-06] v17.59.1 — UX POLISH: Alert HUD Cleanup
//   - Stale alerts now show "NO ACTIVE ALERT" instead of appending [STALE]
//   - Cleaner interface for expired alerts (> 30 minutes old)
//   - No changes to alert firing logic
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.59 CHANGELOG — EMERGENCY METHODOLOGY ALIGNMENT (Direct Trend Override)
// ============================================================================
// [2026-06-06] v17.59 — Direct Trend Logic + Stranded-Price Fix + Reframing
//
// CONTEXT: On a massive H4 bearish breakdown (e.g. NZDUSD), v17.58 displayed
// INVERTED logic (HTF BULLISH + LTF BULLISH + AMD ACCUMULATION) because it
// relied on STALE BOS structural anchors instead of CURRENT price action and
// momentum. v17.59 adds a momentum-first override layer that takes precedence
// over BOS anchors during strong directional expansion.
//
// FIX 1 — DIRECT TREND LOGIC (FORCE RESET) [HIGHEST PRIORITY]
//   • HTF override: if close < H4 SMA50 AND price prints a new 20-bar low →
//     FORCE BEARISH (overrides BOS-derived htfBias). Inverse forces BULLISH.
//   • LTF override: if price is >1.5×ATR below the daily open → FORCE BEARISH.
//     Inverse (>1.5×ATR above day open) forces BULLISH.
//   • Produces finalHTFTrend / finalLTFTrend consumed by HUD + webhook.
//
// FIX 2 — BOS RANGE EXPANSION ("STRANDED PRICE") FIX
//   • The BOS-anchored dealing range now expands EVERY bar on new extremes and
//     a safety clamp guarantees current price is NEVER outside the range.
//   • rangeForceExpanded flag exposes when the safety clamp engaged.
//
// FIX 3 — GUARDIAN REFRAMING (TRAP → TREND EXPANSION)
//   • "TRAP BUY/SELL" relabeled "TREND EXPANSION". During a strong aligned
//     trend, premium/discount location is a CONTINUATION signal (risk 0), not
//     a reversal trap; the discount/premium trap filter is disabled.
//
// FIX 4 — AMD VELOCITY-BASED LOGIC
//   • amdVelocity = (close - close[10]) / max(ATR, mintick) * 100.
//     velocity ≤ -150% → MARKDOWN, ≥ +150% → MARKUP (SPEED beats LOCATION);
//     otherwise falls back to the v17.58 zone-based AMD classifier.
//
// FIX 5 — HUD TRANSPARENCY
//   • New debug rows: Range Anchor (BOS time), Trend Override (HTF/LTF), Strong
//     Trend mode and AMD Velocity. HTF/LTF rows now show the FINAL trend.
//
// WEBHOOK: +9 fields — htf_override_active, ltf_override_active, htf_trend_final,
//   ltf_trend_final, range_anchor_time, range_force_expanded, amd_velocity,
//   strong_trend_mode (guardian_label reframed). Mirrored as hidden plots.
//
// PRESERVED: 5-state sequence machine, BOS-anchored ranges (now with expansion
//   fix), PDH/PDL (v17.57), Guardian HTF gating (v17.56.9), dual mode, visuals.
// ============================================================================
//
// v17.58 CHANGELOG — BOS-ANCHORED RANGE + 5-STATE SEQUENCE GATE  (BREAKING)
// ============================================================================
// [2026-06-06] v17.58 — Structural Range + Institutional Sequence Engine
//
// *** BREAKING CHANGE ***  The H4 premium/discount range is no longer a rolling
// ta.highest/lowest window. It is now anchored to the most recent H4 Break of
// Structure (BOS): origin = swing point before the break, termination = broken
// level extended by a dynamic (ATR-based) expansion. This changes where premium/
// discount/equilibrium fall, which alters POI scoring, AMD, zone visuals and the
// frequency/timing of alerts. Users MUST recreate their TradingView alerts and
// re-validate any backtests after upgrading.
//
// NEW FEATURES:
//   1. BOS-ANCHORED H4 RANGE — request.security("240", ta.pivothigh/pivotlow on
//      closed bars, lookahead_off). Tracks bosTrend, bosOrigin, bosTermination.
//      Overrides h4RangeHigh / h4RangeLow so ALL downstream consumers use it.
//   2. 5-STATE SEQUENCE MACHINE (THE GATE) — State1 LOCATION (premium for shorts
//      / discount for longs) -> State2 LIQUIDITY (sweep) -> State3 DISPLACEMENT
//      (M5 MSS + displacement) -> State4 MITIGATION (retrace into OB/FVG) ->
//      State5 EXECUTION (NY kill zone). When strictSequence=true, alerts are
//      blocked if states are skipped.
//   3. GUARDIAN RECALIBRATION — sweeps are now REQUIRED (not traps); green-light
//      after Sweep + MSS; continuation breaks WITHOUT an LTF shift are blocked.
//      Existing HTF gating (v17.56.9) preserved as the base layer.
//   4. HUD SEQUENCE TRACKER — shows state X/5, per-step checklist, the next
//      missing step, and "READY - WATCH FOR RETRACE" when complete.
//   5. WEBHOOK SEQUENCE FIELDS — sequence_state, sequence_step, missing_step,
//      bos_range_high/low/equilibrium, bos_trend, state1..5 flags,
//      liquidity_swept, ltf_shift_detected, displacement_detected,
//      mitigation_zone appended to the JSON payload.
//
// PRESERVED: PDH/PDL (v17.57), Guardian HTF gating (v17.56.9), dual mode
//            (v17.56.7), session detection, all visuals (FVG, OB, flip zones).
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// v17.57 CHANGELOG — PDH/PDL INSTITUTIONAL LIQUIDITY LEVELS
// ============================================================================
// [2026-06-05] v17.57 — Previous Day High/Low Integration
//
// NEW FEATURE: PDH (Previous Day High) and PDL (Previous Day Low) are now
// fully integrated as institutional liquidity reference levels.
//
// CHANGES:
//   - PDH/PDL computed via request.security("D", high[1]/low[1], lookahead_off)
//   - Chart lines drawn (dashed, color-configurable) with labels
//   - Proximity detection: nearPDH / nearPDL (within 15% of PDH-PDL range)
//   - Sweep detection: pdhSwept / pdlSwept (wick through, close back)
//   - POI score: +1 bonus when price near PDH or PDL
//   - Guardian: sweep flag appended to label when PDH/PDL swept
//   - HUD: new PDH/PDL row with proximity and sweep annotations
//   - Webhook: 6 new optional fields (pdh, pdl, near_pdh, near_pdl, pdh_swept, pdl_swept)
//   - Backend: decoder + /api/signals updated with backward compatibility
//
// UNCHANGED: All entry logic, DT state machine, bias engine, FVG, flip zones,
//            existing alert names, existing webhook fields.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// v17.56.8: CENTRALIZED VERSION MANAGEMENT (single source of truth)
// ============================================================================
// VERSION is a const string (literal assignment) so it can be used in HUD,
// dynamic alert() payloads, and const alertcondition() messages alike.
// NOTE: The indicator() title above must remain a literal (Pine requires the
// declaration statement to be first), so it is kept in sync manually.
string VERSION = "v17.85.65"

// ============================================================================
// v17.56.9 CHANGELOG — GUARDIAN HTF-GATING + RISK FLAG (Guardian safety only)
// ============================================================================
// Minimal, display/messaging-only safety upgrade. NO core trading logic
// changed (entry triggers, alert cooldown, POI scoring, bias engine, FVG/OB,
// flip zones, AMD, alert consistency, sessions, dual-mode all FROZEN).
//
//   1. Guardian HTF-Gate: when a CONTINUATION BUY/SELL Guardian label conflicts
//      with the HTF bias, append "(HTF COUNTER — STANDBY)" so the label cannot
//      mislead. Controlled by input `guardian_require_htf_match` (default true).
//   2. Guardian Risk Flag `guardian_risk` (0=low, 1=medium, 2=high):
//        0 = HTF aligned (or non-continuation state)
//        1 = HTF conflict, alignment not COUNTER TREND (minor mismatch)
//        2 = HTF conflict AND alignment == COUNTER TREND (high risk)
//   3. HUD Guardian row shows the gated label + risk indicator, driven by
//      input `guardian_risk_mode` (0=off, 1=number, 2=colored tag).
//   4. Webhook payload gains two OPTIONAL fields: guardian_label, guardian_risk.
//
// Backward compatible: with guardian_require_htf_match=false the Guardian label
// is byte-for-byte identical to v17.56.8 and guardian_risk is always 0.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// v17.56.8: ALERT CONSISTENCY ENGINE (single source of truth for alerts)
// ============================================================================
// All alert components (direction, setup ID, bias tag, guardian label, message)
// must derive from one validated state. f_validateAlertConsistency() enforces
// that they agree before any alert is allowed to fire.
type AlertState
    string direction      // "LONG" or "SHORT"
    string setupID        // "BULL_..." or "BEAR_..."
    string biasTag        // "BULLISH" or "BEARISH"
    string guardianLabel  // "CONTINUATION LONG" / "CONTINUATION SHORT" / ...
    string alertMessage   // Full JSON payload
    bool   isValid        // Passes consistency check

f_validateAlertConsistency(AlertState state) =>
    bool isConsistent = true
    // Rule 1: Direction must match setup ID prefix
    if state.direction == "LONG" and not str.startswith(state.setupID, "BULL_")
        isConsistent := false
    if state.direction == "SHORT" and not str.startswith(state.setupID, "BEAR_")
        isConsistent := false
    // Rule 2: Guardian label must match direction
    if state.direction == "LONG" and not str.contains(state.guardianLabel, "LONG")
        isConsistent := false
    if state.direction == "SHORT" and not str.contains(state.guardianLabel, "SHORT")
        isConsistent := false
    // Rule 3: Bias tag must align with direction
    if state.direction == "LONG" and state.biasTag != "BULLISH"
        isConsistent := false
    if state.direction == "SHORT" and state.biasTag != "BEARISH"
        isConsistent := false
    isConsistent

// ============================================================================
// v17.54.4 CRITICAL FIX: Force 5000-bar historical buffers for ALL price series
// ============================================================================
// Without these, TradingView auto-sizes buffers to the minimum needed on initial
// load. When zone rendering later requests bar_index values stored hundreds of
// bars ago (via dBar/sBar arrays), the buffer is too small and crashes with:
//   "The requested historical offset (N) is beyond the historical buffer's limit (N-1)"
// Observed on USDCHF 5M — offset 349 vs limit 348.
// Fix: Force 5000-bar buffers for every series that box.new()/line.new() might
// reference indirectly through stored bar_index values.
// ============================================================================
max_bars_back(open, 5000)
max_bars_back(high, 5000)
max_bars_back(low, 5000)
max_bars_back(close, 5000)
max_bars_back(volume, 5000)
max_bars_back(time, 5000)

// v17.56.7: Dual Mode Alert System — DATA/EXECUTION modes, session detection, direction fix, hard block rules.
// v17.56.6: Sniper OTE Upgrade — OTE Depth Scoring Bonus ("Picky Eater" Enhancement).
// v17.56.5: Flip Zone Intelligence — 3-Point Strict Classification for S&D zones.
// v17.56.4: Visual Upgrade — Supply/Demand/OB boxes with enhanced opacity + color coding.
// v17.56.2: MICRO-FIX — HTF Pivot Responsiveness (htfPivotLen 15→8, range 5-15).
// v17.56.1: CRITICAL FIX — Timeframe correction (HTF=H4, LTF=M15), pivot differentiation, HUD fix.
// v17.56.0: HTF Bias Layer — Dual Bias System (Daily + H4 structural bias).
// v17.55.0: Structural BOS H4 bias engine with feature flag (STRUCTURAL/RANGE).
// v17.54.4: HUD safety hardening — f_safeText(), f_setCell() wrappers, bounds checking.
// v17.54.2: Zone age pruning, HUD init outside barstate.islast.
// v17.54.4: Restored max_bars_back for all price series (USDCHF 5M crash fix).

// ============================================================================
// v17.56.7 CHANGELOG — Dual Mode Alert System & Tracker Integrity Upgrade
// ============================================================================
// [2026-06-02] v17.56.7 — ALERT SYSTEM: Dual Mode + Session + Direction Fix
//
// NEW: Dual Mode Alert System (DATA vs EXECUTION)
//   - DATA mode: Fires during London/NY sessions when POI >= 3, not blocked
//   - EXECUTION mode: Fires during NY session when POI >= 5, WITH TREND,
//     Guardian = CONTINUATION BUY/SELL, not blocked
//   - alertMode variable tracks current mode per bar
//
// NEW: Session Detection with Proper EST Timezone Conversion
//   - London Session: 3:00-8:00 EST (using America/New_York timezone)
//   - NY Session: 8:00-12:00 EST
//   - isTradeSession = isLondonSession OR isNYSession
//
// NEW: Hard Block Rules — Prevent Junk Alerts
//   - blockSignal = poiScore == 0 OR actionStep == "INVALIDATED"
//   - All alerts gated by blockSignal check
//
// NEW: Guardian State Validation for EXECUTION Mode
//   - Only "CONTINUATION BUY" and "CONTINUATION SELL" qualify
//   - WAITING, IDLE, TRAP, SNIPER states blocked from EXECUTION
//
// CRITICAL FIX: Direction Validation Against Zone Type
//   - LONG requires: Demand zone OR Bullish OB context
//   - SHORT requires: Supply zone OR Bearish OB context
//   - HTF+LTF must agree on direction
//   - Mismatched direction+zone combinations are hard blocked
//
// UPDATED: Alert JSON Payload — Full context with mode/session/direction
//   - New fields: mode, session, direction, setup, align, htf_bias, ltf_bias
//   - Entry/SL/TP included for trade execution
//   - valid=true flag for tracker integrity
//
// Flip Zones, OTE scoring, FVG boxes, and HUD layout unchanged from v17.56.6.
// ============================================================================

