// ============================================================================
// v17.56.0 CHANGELOG — HTF Bias Layer (Dual Bias System)
// ============================================================================
// [2026-05-29] v17.56.0 — ENHANCEMENT: Daily Structural Bias + Dual Bias HUD
//
// OVERVIEW: Adds a Higher Timeframe (HTF) bias engine using Daily structural
// analysis (f_d1_structure). The existing H4 bias becomes the LTF (Lower
// Timeframe) layer. Both biases display in the HUD for dual-timeframe
// confluence reading. Alignment logic enhanced with WITH TREND / COUNTER TREND.
//
// NEW FUNCTION: f_d1_structure()
//   - Identical logic to f_h4_structure() but evaluated on Daily timeframe
//   - Computes swing structure: HH/HL = bullish, LL/LH = bearish
//   - Called via request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", ...) with lookahead_off
//
// HTF BIAS COMPUTATION:
//   - htfBias (int): 1 = bullish, -1 = bearish, 0 = neutral
//   - htfDirStr: "BULLISH" / "BEARISH" / "NEUTRAL"
//   - htfColor: green / red / gray
//
// HUD CHANGES:
//   - maxHudRows increased 24 → 25 (new row inserted)
//   - Row 1: HTF Bias (NEW — Daily structural bias)
//   - Row 2: LTF Bias (was "Bias" — H4 active bias, renamed)
//   - Row 3: Align (shifted +1, now shows WITH TREND / COUNTER TREND / NEUTRAL)
//   - Rows 4-24: All shifted +1 from previous layout
//
// ALIGNMENT ENHANCEMENT (display only — no trading logic changes):
//   - isWithTrend: HTF and LTF biases agree (same direction)
//   - isCounterTrend: HTF and LTF biases oppose (opposite directions)
//   - Align row shows "WITH TREND ✅" / "COUNTER TREND ⚠️" / "NEUTRAL"
//
// DEBUG: HTF structural debug row added (gated by showDebugRows && structDebug)
//
// NON-BREAKING: No changes to h4ActiveBias pipeline, alerts, Guardian, or zones.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// v17.55.0 CHANGELOG — Structural BOS H4 Bias Engine
// ============================================================================
// [2026-05-29] v17.55.0 — MAJOR: H4 Bias via Break of Structure (BOS)
//
// OVERVIEW: Converts the H4 Bias system from range-location (where price
// sits relative to P&D zone thresholds) to a true structural BOS model:
//   - BULLISH = Higher High + Higher Low confirmed (HH/HL)
//   - BEARISH = Lower Low + Lower High confirmed (LL/LH)
//   - NEUTRAL = no confirmed structural bias yet
//
// NEW FUNCTION: f_h4_structure()
//   - Uses ta.pivothigh/ta.pivotlow with configurable lookback (default 3)
//   - Tracks swing highs/lows and classifies HH/HL/LL/LH patterns
//   - Candle-close confirmation via request.security("240", ...)
//   - lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off for no-repaint guarantee
//   - Returns [bias, lastSwingHigh, lastSwingLow, flipBar] tuple
//
// FEATURE FLAG: h4BiasMode input (H4 Multi-TF Bias group)
//   - "STRUCTURAL" (default): Uses BOS-based structural bias
//   - "RANGE": Preserves v17.54.x range-location behavior
//   - Toggle allows instant rollback if structural model misbehaves
//
// WRAPPER SYSTEM: h4ActiveBias replaces direct h4Bias in all consumers
//   - h4ActiveBias = (mode == STRUCTURAL) ? h4Bias_struct : h4Bias_range
//   - h4ActiveBiasStr, h4ActiveBiasNeutral, h4ActiveBiasChanged helpers
//   - Original h4Bias_range preserved for zone calculations
//
// CONSUMER MIGRATION: All h4Bias references migrated to h4ActiveBias
//   - Guardian, alignment, counter-trend, alert conditions
//   - Invalidation, DT progression, action step, IPM
//   - Zone position detection UNCHANGED (still uses price vs zone boundaries)
//
// HUD UPDATES:
//   - Row 1 "Bias" now shows h4ActiveBias (structural or range per mode)
//   - New debug row "H4Struct" shows structural state when debug enabled
//   - maxHudRows increased 20 → 23 to accommodate structural debug rows
//
// SAFETY:
//   - max_bars_back already covers pivot lookback (5000 >> 3+3)
//   - Historical buffer guards for pivot na values
//   - Feature flag enables instant rollback to range mode
//   - All existing P&D zone calculations preserved as-is
//
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// v17.54.4 CHANGELOG — HUD Safety Hardening (NO logic/filter/alert changes)
// ============================================================================
// [2026-05-27] v17.54.4 — HUD Safety Patterns for Maximum Stability
//
// SAFETY 1: f_safeText() wrapper function
//   - Returns "—" for na/null values, prevents na-crash in HUD text
//   - Applied to ALL dynamic string values before HUD cell writes
//
// SAFETY 2: f_setCell() / f_setHdrCell() / f_setDbgCell() wrapper functions
//   - Bounds-check column and row indices against maxHudCols/maxHudRows
//   - na-check table reference before every write
//   - Prevents array out-of-bounds and cell update failures
//   - Three variants: standard (size.normal), header (size.normal), debug (size.tiny)
//
// SAFETY 3: Hard limit constants
//   - maxHudRows = 20, maxHudCols = 2 (exact fit for 20-row HUD, see Row Map)
//   - All cell writes validated against these limits
//
// SAFETY 4: HUD initialization guard (reinforced from v17.54.2)
//   - var table hud = na at global scope
//   - table.new() only called if na(hud) — guaranteed single creation
//   - barstate.islast block gated by not na(hud)
//
// ============================================================================
// v17.54.2 CHANGELOG — Stability & HUD Fix (NO logic/filter/alert changes)
// ============================================================================
// [2026-05-27] v17.54.2 — Stability & HUD Reliability Fix
//
// BUG FIX: "Indicator error" crash on data-dense charts (5M USDJPY)
//   - Removed global max_bars_back=5000 from indicator() — forced 5000-bar buffers
//     on ALL variables, exceeding TradingView memory limits on dense timeframes
//   - Removed max_bars_back(time, 5000) global override
//   - Added targeted max_bars_back only on zone bar-index arrays that need it
//
// BUG FIX: HUD table disappearing intermittently
//   - Moved `var table hud = table.new(...)` OUTSIDE barstate.islast block
//   - Table object now created once on first bar (var), populated on last bar
//   - Prevents HUD from vanishing during chart navigation/replay
//
// OPTIMIZATION: Zone rendering loops
//   - Added empty-array guards to skip zone drawing when no zones exist
//   - Added zone age pruning: zones older than 500 bars auto-removed to prevent
